ail":"guilhermesin2011@gmail.com","name":"Guilherme Ferreira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T12:57:19Z","email":"guilhermesin2011@gmail.com","name":"Guilherme Ferreira"},"message":"docs: add ecosystem VitePress Pages site, brand mark, and README\n\nReplace the legacy masterclass Pages surface with audit-backed /en+/pt docs,\nCI deploy workflow, update-gh-pages agent prompt, and PromptDesk SVG branding.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"f1af7958d94f916c79d1b1db5476da7f1f957280","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guilheeeeeeerme/promptdesk/git/trees/f1af7958d94f916c79d1b1db5476da7f1f957280"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guilheeeeeeerme/promptdesk/git/commits/a43ece53fd968c83677abbd4fa3bb9086d20f1d6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2565469?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Guilheeeeeeerme","id":2565469,"login":"Guilheeeeeeerme","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjU0Njk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Guilheeeeeeerme/promptdesk/commit/a43ece53fd968c83677abbd4fa3bb9086d20f1d6","node_id":"C_kwDOURHTrdoAKGE0M2VjZTUzZmQ5NjhjODM2NzdhYmJkNGZhM2JiOTA4NmQyMGYxZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Guilheeeeeeerme/promptdesk/commit/c3e9da1fdcca6dcce9c73186e10e109a84044d7e","sha":"c3e9da1fdcca6dcce9c73186e10e109a84044d7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guilheeeeeeerme/promptdesk/commits/c3e9da1fdcca6dcce9c73186e10e109a84044d7e"}],"sha":"a43ece53fd968c83677abbd4fa3bb9086d20f1d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guilheeeeeeerme/promptdesk/commits/a43ece53fd968c83677abbd4fa3bb9086d20f1d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2565469?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Guilheeeeeeerme","id":2565469,"login":"Guilheeeeeeerme","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjU0Njk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guilheeeeeeerme","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guilheeeeeeerme/promptdesk/commits/c3e9da1fdcca6dcce9c73186e10e109a84044d7e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T12:32:26Z","email":"ferreiraga@outlook.com","name":"Guilherme"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T12:32:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): harden LLM boundaries per OWASP LLM Top 10 2026 (#12)\n\n* fix(security): harden LLM boundaries per OWASP LLM Top 10 2026\n\nPrompt injection (LLM01): buildSupportPrompt placed the support payload\nbetween BEGIN/END_UNTRUSTED_SUPPORT_CONTEXT markers. JSON encoding\nescapes quotes and newlines but leaves the marker text intact, so a\nguideline or agent request containing the closing marker escaped the data\nblock and had its remaining text read as instructions. Add\nneutralizeUntrusted, which defangs the markers and strips invisible\ncharacters (Unicode tag block, zero-width, bidi overrides), and apply it\nto the payload.\n\nThe guideline validation template fed uploaded guideline text to the\nvalidator with no delimiter at all, so an upload could argue its own case\nto the model. Fence and neutralize it. The deterministic screen in\nGuidelineValidator remains the control that decides; this only stops the\nadvisory model from being addressed directly.\n\nImproper output handling (LLM10): generated replies were persisted and\npublished with no output-side screen, while uploaded guidelines were\nscreened on the way in. A support agent may paste a reply to a customer,\nso a covert tracking pixel or exfiltration link in generated text is a\nlive channel out of the tenant. Screen replies for script, exfiltration,\nand tracking payloads after placeholder substitution.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): fail closed on OutputPolicyError without LLM failover\n\nPolicy blocks must halt once (OWASP LLM10/LLM06): mark the message failed,\npublish failure, and return — do not failover or rethrow into BullMQ retry.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"366a39600e1de5ef2cb7380b4da72e4934f2898f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guilheeeeeeerme/promptdesk/git/trees/366a39600e1de5ef2cb7380b4da72e4934f2898f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guilheeeeeeerme/promptdesk/git/commits/c3e9da1fdcca6dcce9c73186e10e109a84044d7e","verification":{"payload":"tree 366a39600e1de5ef2cb7380b4da72e4934f2898f\nparent 4aec09ad17228c2624eda5fb8efc95f950bff972\nauthor Guilherme <ferreiraga@outlook.com> 1789389146 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789389146 -0300\n\nfix(security): harden LLM boundaries per OWASP LLM Top 10 2026 (#12)\n\n* fix(security): harden LLM boundaries per OWASP LLM Top 10 2026\n\nPrompt injection (LLM01): buildSupportPrompt placed the support payload\nbetween BEGIN/END_UNTRUSTED_SUPPORT_CONTEXT markers. JSON encoding\nescapes quotes and newlines but leaves the marker text intact, so a\nguideline or agent request containing the closing marker escaped the data\nblock and had its remaining text read as instructions. Add\nneutralizeUntrusted, which defangs the markers and strips invisible\ncharacters (Unicode tag block, zero-width, bidi overrides), and apply it\nto the payload.\n\nThe guideline validation template fed uploaded guideline text to the\nvalidator with no delimiter at all, so an upload could argue its own case\nto the model. Fence and neutralize it. The deterministic screen in\nGuidelineValidator remains the control that decides; this only stops the\nadvisory model from being addressed directly.\n\nImproper output handling (LLM10): generated replies were persisted and\npublished with no output-side screen, while uploaded guidelines were\nscreened on the way in. A support agent may paste a reply to a customer,\nso a covert tracking pixel or exfiltration link in generated text is a\nlive channel out of the tenant. Screen replies for script, exfiltration,\nand tracking payloads after placeholder substitution.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): fail closed on OutputPolicyError without LLM failover\n\nPolicy blocks must halt once (OWASP LLM10/LLM06): mark the message failed,\npublish failure, and return — do not failover or rethrow into BullMQ retry.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthro