"name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:33:46.883Z","repositoryId":1360161003,"sha":"24b100724b658314968fc4ee576674b417075de1"},{"author":{"account":null,"email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-07T11:45:49Z","committedDate":"2026-09-07T11:45:49Z","committer":{"account":null,"email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:33:46.883Z","repositoryId":1360161003,"sha":"8147447d6f4cfce90bb468fa0c6d2f81c75105aa"},{"author":{"account":null,"email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-07T11:30:01Z","committedDate":"2026-09-07T11:30:01Z","committer":{"account":null,"email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:33:46.883Z","repositoryId":1360161003,"sha":"0f95b8e9245e64a3436a7e3b8b61ad7ed18f5fbb"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:33:46.883Z","raw":[{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/6c1c20da187306733dbc3b92d558148456791ee1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T10:59:43Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T10:59:43Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"Name components in minified production builds, from the bundle''s source map\n\nThe tool was close to useless on a staging build: React is production, so the panel showed the\nminified names. It can now map them back, on demand.\n\n- src/sourcemap.ts: VLQ decode, mappings grid, greatest-mapping-at-or-before lookup,\n  sourceMappingURL resolution (including data: maps) and identifierOffset.\n- Two additive bridge commands (protocol stays 2), through the shared runCommand so the channel\n  and relay paths get them: functionSource(instanceId) returns the component function''s own\n  toString() (unwrapping memo/forwardRef), and fetchText(url) fetches a same-origin URL in the\n  page, which is the only place the bundle and its map are reachable. info() also lists the page''s\n  scripts.\n- The panel''s production banner gains \"Resolve names\": for each distinct name it finds the\n  function text in the bundle, turns the offset of its identifier into a line and column, and\n  reads the original name out of the map, then relabels the tree, offenders, fixes, commits and\n  stream, keeping the minified name in a tooltip. Never automatic: it downloads the bundle.\n- Honest about what it cannot do, rather than guessing: a memo(function X(){}) usually loses its\n  identifier to the minifier (those keep displayName), and text that occurs twice is ambiguous.\n\nTwo bugs the new end-to-end test found, both pre-existing:\n- The relay client posted every batch with keepalive, which the Fetch standard caps at 64 KB of\n  body and fails the request over, silently. Source maps and batches with large props never\n  arrived. Only small batches use it now, so an unloading page still flushes.\n- installRerenderLens(page) did not typecheck against a current Playwright Page, which returns a\n  disposable from addInitScript. The documented snippet compiles again.\n\nnpm run e2e:prod (in CI) drives the real thing: the example built by vite build with source maps,\nserved by vite preview, the library injected, the panel resolving ed and fd back to Row and App.\nThe example''s own build script typechecks again (it lacked the vite/client reference).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"3d7dcda1407dcf8b5f8459a7e31009c65d3704c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/3d7dcda1407dcf8b5f8459a7e31009c65d3704c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/6c1c20da187306733dbc3b92d558148456791ee1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/6c1c20da187306733dbc3b92d558148456791ee1","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKDZjMWMyMGRhMTg3MzA2NzMzZGJjM2I5MmQ1NTgxNDg0NTY3OTFlZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/babfe64c535ce99205a2706878f25d3bd4b902ba","sha":"babfe64c535ce99205a2706878f25d3bd4b902ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/babfe64c535ce99205a2706878f25d3bd4b902ba"}],"sha":"6c1c20da187306733dbc3b92d558148456791ee1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/6c1c20da187306733dbc3b92d558148456791ee1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/babfe64c535ce99205a2706878f25d3bd4b902ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T10:22:22Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T10:22:22Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"Release 0.7.0; a mismatched release tag now fails instead of half-succeeding\n\n- package.json and the manifest go to 0.7.0, and the eleven unreleased entries become one 0.7.0\n  section with highlights. 0.6.0 is skipped: the v0.6.0 tag points at the multi-app relay commit,\n  whose package.json still said 0.5.0, so nothing was published under it and reusing the number\n  would make the tag disagree with its artifacts.\n- The release workflow now fails immediately when the tag does not match the package version,\n  instead of building a release named after the wrong version and silently skipping npm. The fix\n  it prints is \"npm version, push, retag\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"78b0ad7984e9f110b13ac0f5ff26896251f0bfa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/78b0ad7984e9f110b13ac0f5ff26896251f0bfa9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/babfe64c535ce99205a2706878f25d3bd4b902ba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/babfe64c535ce99205a2706878f25d3bd4b902ba","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKGJhYmZlNjRjNTM1Y2U5OTIwNWEyNzA2ODc4ZjI1ZDNiZDRiOTAyYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/60d8f62fdcb16291a6352926c0cad25980dc75cc","sha":"60d8f62fdcb16291a6352926c0cad25980dc75cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/60d8f62fdcb16291a6352926c0cad25980dc75cc"}],"sha":"babfe64c535ce99205a2706878f25d3bd4b902ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/babfe64c535ce99205a2706878f25d3bd4b902ba"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/60d8f62fdcb16291a6352926c0cad25980dc75cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T09:54:29Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T09:54:29Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"Milestone T: relay token, nightly cost job; and the panel explains what it is not tracking\n\nHardening:\n- The relay authenticates whenever it is not on loopback. `rerender-lens panel --host 0.0.0.0`\n  generates a token, prints it inside the URL and refuses /events, /message and /status without it\n  (query parameter or x-rerender-lens-token header); the static panel files stay open so the page\n  can load before it authenticates. Both clients split the token out of the URL they are handed,\n  so the printed URL is the only thing a user copies. --token sets your own, --no-token opts out\n  with a warning, loopback is unchanged. Reports carry the app''s prop, state and context values,\n  which is why this matters.\n- e2e/perf.spec.ts + a nightly workflow record what a commit costs at 3,000 and 10,000 memoized\n  rows and fail on a per-size budget. About 32 ms at both sizes: flat, because the per-commit cap\n  stops the walk. The numbers go to the run summary.\n- Audit: no eval outside chrome.devtools.inspectedWindow.eval, no remote code, MV3''s default CSP;\n  documented in the extension README. Failing CI on web-ext lint warnings is left for a CI run to\n  baseline: web-ext cannot execute in this sandbox, so there was nothing to flip against.\n\nWhy is this component not tracked:\n- explainTracking() in the tracker gives a verdict (tracked, reason, fix) mirroring shouldTrack''s\n  rule order, and the state counts distinct rendered vs tracked components (capped at 500).\n  info().tracking, inspect(node).tracking and a new explain() bridge command carry it, through the\n  shared runCommand so the channel and relay paths get it too. Protocol stays 2.\n- The panel''s empty state now says what is being tracked and how many components rendered\n  untracked, with one-click \"Track every component\" and \"Track components matching...\". The\n  Elements sidebar shows the verdict for the selected node with a \"Track this component\" button.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"58e7ed4d80968614e2bbc2a3a83563ac3f178efb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/58e7ed4d80968614e2bbc2a3a83563ac3f178efb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/60d8f62fdcb16291a6352926c0cad25980dc75cc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/60d8f62fdcb16291a6352926c0cad25980dc75cc","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKDYwZDhmNjJmZGNiMTYyOTFhNjM1MjkyNmMwY2FkMjU5ODBkYzc1Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/2464074adf404759897c464622fd4d4ca8d69cfc","sha":"2464074adf404759897c464622fd4d4ca8d69cfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/2464074adf404759897c464622fd4d4ca8d69cfc"}],"sha":"60d8f62fdcb16291a6352926c0cad25980dc75cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/60d8f62fdcb16291a6352926c0cad25980dc75cc"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/2464074adf404759897c464622fd4d4ca8d69cfc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:54:20Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:54:20Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"Milestone S: the docs site as a product page\n\n- scripts/build-docs.mjs now builds four pages plus a demo instead of one long scroll: a landing\n  page that answers \"how do I start with my bundler\" (Vite, Next.js, Webpack, any app through the\n  relay, the extension, tests) with the snippets lifted out of the README by heading so they cannot\n  drift, the README as the guide, the extension guide, and api.html.\n- scripts/docs-api.mjs generates the API reference from the public entry points with the TypeScript\n  compiler already in devDependencies: no documentation toolchain, and the same design as the rest\n  of the site. 155 exports across seven entry points.\n- docs-site/demo/ is a copy of the panel running its demo data, so the site can be clicked before\n  anything is installed.\n- The Pages workflow also builds on a published release, and a release recaptures the screenshots\n  first so they never show an old panel. Screenshots regenerated (they now include the timeline).\n- docs/PLAN.md rewritten: what shipped since 0.5.0, what is left of O, then T and U.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"1e52772c3630657f3a783501b3b526fc1100d456","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/1e52772c3630657f3a783501b3b526fc1100d456"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/2464074adf404759897c464622fd4d4ca8d69cfc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/2464074adf404759897c464622fd4d4ca8d69cfc","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKDI0NjQwNzRhZGY0MDQ3NTk4OTdjNDY0NjIyZmQ0ZDRjYThkNjljZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/751f53f039d08175891404c66bd8f8c112b3ea8a","sha":"751f53f039d08175891404c66bd8f8c112b3ea8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/751f53f039d08175891404c66bd8f8c112b3ea8a"}],"sha":"2464074adf404759897c464622fd4d4ca8d69cfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/2464074adf404759897c464622fd4d4ca8d69cfc"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/751f53f039d08175891404c66bd8f8c112b3ea8a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:10:25Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:10:25Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"Milestone R: several apps on one relay, a commit timeline, settings parity\n\n- Relay: each app stream gets an id and a label (its address, from ?label= or the Origin header).\n  The relay greets the app with its id, the library posts to /message?app=<id>, and the relay\n  stamps `app` on what that app sends to panels and on the roster it sends them. A command\n  carrying `app` goes to that one app; without it, or when that app is gone, to all of them, so\n  an older panel or library behaves as before and the protocol stays at 2.\n- Panel: a picker appears next to the status when more than one app is connected, listing each by\n  address. It watches one at a time, drops the other apps'' reports, addresses its commands, and\n  starts over on the app you switch to. e2e: two pages of the Next example on one relay (a new\n  /admin route), each showing only its own components.\n- Panel: a commit timeline strip above the tree. One bar per commit, height on a sqrt scale of the\n  render count, filled with the avoidable share. Click a bar to open that commit; drag to brush a\n  time window and the tree, Offenders, Fixes, Commits and the stream all narrow to it, with a chip\n  and Esc to clear. Collapsible and persisted, capped at 200 bars, drawn on the existing throttle.\n  The flood demo now spreads receivedAt so the strip is not one bar.\n- The side panel and the DevTools panel are proven to share per-origin settings in both directions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"71373aa32bd0726c83b9368f34fc6417afd6af4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/71373aa32bd0726c83b9368f34fc6417afd6af4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/751f53f039d08175891404c66bd8f8c112b3ea8a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/751f53f039d08175891404c66bd8f8c112b3ea8a","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKDc1MWY1M2YwMzlkMDgxNzU4OTE0MDRjNjZiZDhmOGMxMTJiM2VhOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/17137599bdd7e359539513be382c6a6c41c4a848","sha":"17137599bdd7e359539513be382c6a6c41c4a848","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/17137599bdd7e359539513be382c6a6c41c4a848"}],"sha":"751f53f039d08175891404c66bd8f8c112b3ea8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/751f53f039d08175891404c66bd8f8c112b3ea8a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/17137599bdd7e359539513be382c6a6c41c4a848/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:43:02Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:43:02Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"Milestone Q: Jest integration, React 17 in CI, one runner-report implementation\n\n- rerender-lens/jest and rerender-lens/jest/setup: one setupFilesAfterEnv line collects every\n  avoidable re-render; the reporter prints the run''s ranked fixes and root causes, writes a\n  panel-compatible export and fails the run on a budget violation (Jest ignores process.exitCode\n  under forceExit, so it also implements getLastError). The runner-agnostic half moved to\n  src/runner-report.ts and both integrations share it; rerender-lens/vitest is unchanged.\n- test/jest/ is a real Jest app (jsdom, babel-jest, the package resolved by name through the\n  exports map) driven by scripts/jest-check.mjs: it asserts a strict budget exits non-zero with\n  the offenders listed and a fitting budget exits 0. Its own CI job.\n- npm run test:react17 joins test:react18 in the react-compat CI job, so `react >= 16.8` is a\n  tested claim. The harness is now version-agnostic: test/react-act.ts takes act from react or\n  react-dom/test-utils, and test/react17-client-shim.ts stands in for the root API React 17 does\n  not have. Tests needing a newer React are guarded by the flags in test/react-version.ts.\n- What React 17 cannot do is documented (README compatibility table) and said once at runtime:\n  React records the value read from a context on the fiber only from 18 on, so on 17 a context\n  change is a plain parent re-render; updaters and effect loops need React 18 updater tracking.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"2927cefaa0ffca65f0153291a715314519ab07fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/2927cefaa0ffca65f0153291a715314519ab07fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/17137599bdd7e359539513be382c6a6c41c4a848","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/17137599bdd7e359539513be382c6a6c41c4a848","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKDE3MTM3NTk5YmRkN2UzNTk1Mzk1MTNiZTM4MmM2YTZjNDFjNGE4NDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/c08e3f62d1d653441800fbc29a91bb9db783a222","sha":"c08e3f62d1d653441800fbc29a91bb9db783a222","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/c08e3f62d1d653441800fbc29a91bb9db783a222"}],"sha":"17137599bdd7e359539513be382c6a6c41c4a848","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/17137599bdd7e359539513be382c6a6c41c4a848"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/c08e3f62d1d653441800fbc29a91bb9db783a222/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:16:28Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:16:28Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"Milestones O (code) and P: report-a-problem link, verdicts on modern React\n\n- Panel Settings gains a Help section with \"Report a problem\": a GitHub issue prefilled with the\n  extension and library versions, React version, options, overhead, truncation count and buffer\n  totals, nothing from the page. QA.md gains scale, relay and help checks.\n- test/modern.test.ts pins the verdict for React Compiler output, use(promise), startTransition,\n  Suspense fallback -> content, useSyncExternalStore selectors, render props, forwardRef + memo\n  refs, classes with shouldComponentUpdate, useDeferredValue and useId (React 19-only cases skip\n  on the React 18 run). examples/vite-react/modern.html has the same shapes.\n- Library fixes from the matrix: compiled components (detected via the useMemoCache slots on the\n  fiber) carry `compiled: true` and a parent-triggered render with identical props is not\n  avoidable; content re-rendered because a Suspense boundary above resolved is explained, not\n  flagged; a new ref object per render reports `deep-equal` on `ref` with useRef advice instead\n  of a spurious ref.current change; the deferred useDeferredValue render is a hooks render and\n  never an effect loop; classes get PureComponent / shouldComponentUpdate advice.\n- README: \"What counts as avoidable\" table; CLAUDE.md design decisions; CHANGELOG.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"5be0809c64a60527ff3d9586ca5bc9625deb0c38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/5be0809c64a60527ff3d9586ca5bc9625deb0c38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/c08e3f62d1d653441800fbc29a91bb9db783a222","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/c08e3f62d1d653441800fbc29a91bb9db783a222","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKGMwOGUzZjYyZDFkNjUzNDQxODAwZmJjMjlhOTFiYjlkYjc4M2EyMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/15db6ed4ced03423f08e2804bb0c3814106a1958","sha":"15db6ed4ced03423f08e2804bb0c3814106a1958","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/15db6ed4ced03423f08e2804bb0c3814106a1958"}],"sha":"c08e3f62d1d653441800fbc29a91bb9db783a222","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/c08e3f62d1d653441800fbc29a91bb9db783a222"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/15db6ed4ced03423f08e2804bb0c3814106a1958/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:52:23Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:52:23Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"README half the length; docs site with hero, sticky contents and cleaner layout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"d9cd34b3b4821a86f38124d29516b541392754eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/d9cd34b3b4821a86f38124d29516b541392754eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/15db6ed4ced03423f08e2804bb0c3814106a1958","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/15db6ed4ced03423f08e2804bb0c3814106a1958","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKDE1ZGI2ZWQ0Y2VkMDM0MjNmMDhlMjgwNGJiMGMzODE0MTA2YTE5NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/609a2a8813e3adc0b561d6d584d9e781b6d447a9","sha":"609a2a8813e3adc0b561d6d584d9e781b6d447a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/609a2a8813e3adc0b561d6d584d9e781b6d447a9"}],"sha":"15db6ed4ced03423f08e2804bb0c3814106a1958","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/15db6ed4ced03423f08e2804bb0c3814106a1958"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/609a2a8813e3adc0b561d6d584d9e781b6d447a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:47:35Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:47:35Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"docs: plan after 0.5.0 (milestones O–T)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"15dec6d46d4c96ca5f3ac2dff4338b6a0e9eb115","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/15dec6d46d4c96ca5f3ac2dff4338b6a0e9eb115"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/609a2a8813e3adc0b561d6d584d9e781b6d447a9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/609a2a8813e3adc0b561d6d584d9e781b6d447a9","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKDYwOWEyYTg4MTNlM2FkYzBiNTYxZDZkNTg0ZDllNzgxYjZkNDQ3YTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/c75b09bdd1ead90098022e3904961fbd20178faa","sha":"c75b09bdd1ead90098022e3904961fbd20178faa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/c75b09bdd1ead90098022e3904961fbd20178faa"}],"sha":"609a2a8813e3adc0b561d6d584d9e781b6d447a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/609a2a8813e3adc0b561d6d584d9e781b6d447a9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/c75b09bdd1ead90098022e3904961fbd20178faa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:43:31Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:43:31Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"Milestone N: Web Store assets by script, panel flood e2e, release 0.5.0\n\n- scripts/store-media.mjs (npm run store:media): five 1280x800 screenshots of the panel''s demo\n  data (report, offenders, commits, fixes in dark, sessions) and the 440x280 / 1400x560 promo\n  tiles, committed under extension/store/media/. LISTING.md and PUBLISHING.md point at them;\n  the listing also mentions sessions and the side panel / window modes.\n- e2e: panel.html?demo&flood=20000 must switch views, filter and answer the event loop within\n  budgets (it does in ~3 s end to end).\n- 0.5.0: package.json + manifest, CHANGELOG section with highlights.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"0b61dc32caebe782328c77ca5b33dfcde6a97722","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/0b61dc32caebe782328c77ca5b33dfcde6a97722"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/c75b09bdd1ead90098022e3904961fbd20178faa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/c75b09bdd1ead90098022e3904961fbd20178faa","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKGM3NWIwOWJkZDFlYWQ5MDA5ODAyMmUzOTA0OTYxZmJkMjAxNzhmYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/056e38b76bd782e63248c787062ced00fbebebfb","sha":"056e38b76bd782e63248c787062ced00fbebebfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/056e38b76bd782e63248c787062ced00fbebebfb"}],"sha":"c75b09bdd1ead90098022e3904961fbd20178faa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/c75b09bdd1ead90098022e3904961fbd20178faa"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/056e38b76bd782e63248c787062ced00fbebebfb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:55:15Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:55:15Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"Milestone M: React 18 in CI, root causes in the library and CLI, live info in the panel\n\n- npm run test:react18 + CI job: the unit suite against React 18 through\n  test/react-compat.config.ts (aliases react/react-dom/JSX runtimes to .react18/). Found and\n  fixed: the custom hook name replay counted React 18''s own `useState` wrapper frame as a custom\n  hook; frames named like a React primitive are skipped now.\n- src/causes.ts: the panel''s commit/root-cause analysis (analyzeCommit, rootCauseOf,\n  contextAttribution, cascadeTree, rootCauseSummary) moved into the library, typed over\n  ReportLike, plus groupByCommit / rankRootCauses / formatRootCauses. formatFixes ends with a\n  \"Root causes\" section when reports carry commitId; `rerender-lens causes export.json` prints\n  it alone. The panel imports the shared code (-136 lines).\n- The panel re-reads info() every 3 s while connected (overhead, truncated banner, enabled).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"e9ca50ef8de041c7fc18f25987a637bfae692312","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/e9ca50ef8de041c7fc18f25987a637bfae692312"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/056e38b76bd782e63248c787062ced00fbebebfb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/056e38b76bd782e63248c787062ced00fbebebfb","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKDA1NmUzOGI3NmJkNzgyZTYzMjQ4Yzc4NzA2MmNlZDAwZmJlYmViZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/ef22b151c8b00ae52ff7689eb549b7da85ada698","sha":"ef22b151c8b00ae52ff7689eb549b7da85ada698","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/ef22b151c8b00ae52ff7689eb549b7da85ada698"}],"sha":"056e38b76bd782e63248c787062ced00fbebebfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/056e38b76bd782e63248c787062ced00fbebebfb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/ef22b151c8b00ae52ff7689eb549b7da85ada698/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:12:52Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:12:52Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"Milestone L: one analysis implementation, Next.js verified end to end, built-artifact tests in CI\n\n- The panel imports fixes, session summaries and diff paths from src/ (typed over a structural\n  ReportLike) instead of keeping its own copies: panel.ts -330 lines; library fixes gain the\n  snippets and context/provider attribution the panel had, ranked fixes carry their reports.\n- examples/next: App Router app started from instrumentation-client.ts with rerender-lens/setup,\n  reporting to the relay panel via NEXT_PUBLIC_RERENDER_LENS_RELAY. e2e/next.spec.ts +\n  e2e/next.config.ts (npm run e2e:next; CI job e2e-next) start the relay and next dev and check\n  the panel connects, replays the buffer, streams live reports and highlights back into the app.\n- Bugs it found: rerender-lens/setup read process.env[key] dynamically, which bundlers never\n  inline (the relay env var was invisible and the entry ran in production builds); the relay\n  did not greet a panel that connected after the app, and the panel sent its first command\n  before its stream was open, losing the reply to the connection race. The relay now sends the\n  app count to each new panel; the panel attaches on that greeting. /favicon.ico answers 204.\n- npm run test:built (check + CI) runs the vendor-script test after the build; the default e2e\n  config matches only extension.spec.ts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"68ed59510b5f3c43e2a1fbc67c7f42edb1487666","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/68ed59510b5f3c43e2a1fbc67c7f42edb1487666"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/ef22b151c8b00ae52ff7689eb549b7da85ada698","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/ef22b151c8b00ae52ff7689eb549b7da85ada698","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKGVmMjJiMTUxYzhiMDBhZTUyZmY3Njg5ZWI1NDliN2RhODVhZGE2OTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/d769b8746e01e5c9822e2e7a41daea6ec5dbfd8e","sha":"d769b8746e01e5c9822e2e7a41daea6ec5dbfd8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/d769b8746e01e5c9822e2e7a41daea6ec5dbfd8e"}],"sha":"ef22b151c8b00ae52ff7689eb549b7da85ada698","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/ef22b151c8b00ae52ff7689eb549b7da85ada698"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/d769b8746e01e5c9822e2e7a41daea6ec5dbfd8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T12:14:32Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T12:18:17Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"Publishing notes: bump package.json before tagging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"f0355814bc170819f215cd10859f183cd617d7d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/f0355814bc170819f215cd10859f183cd617d7d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/d769b8746e01e5c9822e2e7a41daea6ec5dbfd8e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/d769b8746e01e5c9822e2e7a41daea6ec5dbfd8e","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKGQ3NjliODc0NmUwMWU1Yzk4MjJlMmU3YTQxZGFlYTZlYzVkYmZkOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/76b679460a568b32d78c7a9b360c687ad4cf2a6f","sha":"76b679460a568b32d78c7a9b360c687ad4cf2a6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/76b679460a568b32d78c7a9b360c687ad4cf2a6f"}],"sha":"d769b8746e01e5c9822e2e7a41daea6ec5dbfd8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/d769b8746e01e5c9822e2e7a41daea6ec5dbfd8e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/76b679460a568b32d78c7a9b360c687ad4cf2a6f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T12:14:01Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T12:18:17Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"Release workflow: skip npm publish for an already-published version, warn on tag/version mismatch\n\nv0.3.3 and v0.3.4 pointed at commits whose package.json still said 0.3.0 (published by v0.3.2),\nso npm publish rejected the duplicate and the GitHub release step never ran. The release with\nthe extension zips is now created either way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"abfd92a0f0bb2d77d75eb6d1732ae5ae3c784fb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/abfd92a0f0bb2d77d75eb6d1732ae5ae3c784fb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/76b679460a568b32d78c7a9b360c687ad4cf2a6f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/76b679460a568b32d78c7a9b360c687ad4cf2a6f","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKDc2YjY3OTQ2MGE1NjhiMzJkNzhjN2E5YjM2MGM2ODdhZDRjZjJhNmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/c2bbd9e2d3a7135f963e0576b16eaac07b3bcb55","sha":"c2bbd9e2d3a7135f963e0576b16eaac07b3bcb55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/c2bbd9e2d3a7135f963e0576b16eaac07b3bcb55"}],"sha":"76b679460a568b32d78c7a9b360c687ad4cf2a6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/76b679460a568b32d78c7a9b360c687ad4cf2a6f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/c2bbd9e2d3a7135f963e0576b16eaac07b3bcb55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T11:51:29Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T12:18:17Z","email":"palanisamy.muthusamy@zoominfo.com","name":"Palanisamy Muthusamy"},"message":"Milestone K: scale test, truncation readout in the panel, release 0.4.0\n\n- examples/vite-react/scale.html?rows=N: N memoized cells sharing a 2,000-item context value and\n  a 4 MB typed-array prop, all re-rendering avoidably per parent update, with a readout of\n  info().overhead and info().truncated. The Vite plugin injects the library there too.\n- e2e: the scale page with 3,000 rows stays responsive after three full re-renders; the cap\n  reports the first 200 cells per commit and counts the rest; the buffer stays bounded.\n- Panel: the skipped-report count from info().truncated shows in the status tooltip and as a\n  banner with the remedy (narrow include, or fix the top offenders).\n- Release 0.4.0: package.json and manifest bumped, CHANGELOG section with highlights, docs media\n  regenerated from the trimmed panel, README/CLAUDE.md mention the scale page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114APukjwqCYqnVgfz7viMP","tree":{"sha":"458121396b73458cfdc32e0ae9f810979bccc516","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/458121396b73458cfdc32e0ae9f810979bccc516"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/c2bbd9e2d3a7135f963e0576b16eaac07b3bcb55","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/c2bbd9e2d3a7135f963e0576b16eaac07b3bcb55","node_id":"C_kwDOURJo69oAKGMyYmJkOWUyZDNhNzEzNWY5NjNlMDU3NmIxNmVhYWMwN2IzYmNiNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commit/52fe642f30f174270b96a92740845a37fc8d9ea0","sha":"52fe642f30f174270b96a92740845a37fc8d9ea0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/52fe642f30f174270b96a92740845a37fc8d9ea0"}],"sha":"c2bbd9e2d3a7135f963e0576b16eaac07b3bcb55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/c2bbd9e2d3a7135f963e0576b16eaac07b3bcb55"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17231446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/palanisamym14/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/palanisamym14/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/palanisamym14/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/palanisamym14/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/palanisamym14","id":17231446,"login":"palanisamym14","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjMxNDQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/palanisamym14/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/palanisamym14/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/palanisamym14/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/palanisamym14/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/palanisamym14/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/palanisamym14","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/commits/52fe642f30f174270b96a92740845a37fc8d9ea0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T11:54:45Z","email":"palanisamym14@gmail.com","name":"palanisamym14"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T11:54:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Docs workflow: drop configure-pages enablement\n\nCreating a Pages site needs Administration: write, which GITHUB_TOKEN cannot have, so enablement: true always failed with Resource not accessible by integration. Pages is now enabled in repo settings with source GitHub Actions.\r\n\r\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\r\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J9ZS412gKzQPc8DaXG5JWS","tree":{"sha":"fb4fe12023a70a2626efa0621557ea89d18cf8fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/trees/fb4fe12023a70a2626efa0621557ea89d18cf8fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NexaLeaf/rerender-lens/git/commits/52fe642f30f174270b96a92740845a37fc8d9ea0","verification":{"payload":"tree fb4fe12023a70a2626efa0621557ea89d18cf8fd\nparent e23da14a87492f2bf773e107b7a1f000c71a0762\nauthor palanisamym14 <palanisamym14@gmail.com> 1788868485 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788868485 +0530\n\nDocs workflow: drop configure-pages enablement\n\nCreating a Pages site needs Administration: write, which GITHUB_TOKEN cannot have, so enablement: true always failed with Resource not accessible by integration. Pages is now enabled in repo settings with source GitHub Actions.\r\n\r\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\r\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J9ZS412gKzQPc8DaXG5JWS","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn/eFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkrQQAJcZ0GEta7+aV9ab0CduuULt\nDD6mn94kDoz1