://api.github.com/users/hakangenc1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakangenc1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakangenc1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakangenc1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakangenc1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hakangenc1/MF-Modern.js-v3/commits/b37ae74c8f5b70a5968af6b0eb478fed0c22c225/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T11:13:35Z","email":"sanials4life2@gmail.com","name":"Hakan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T11:13:35Z","email":"sanials4life2@gmail.com","name":"Hakan"},"message":"fix(shell): a cold remote must not crash the SSR host\n\nOn free hosting the remotes spin down after ~15 min idle. When the shell then\nSSR-loads a cold remote, the host returns an HTML \"waking up\" page instead of\nthe manifest JSON; MF''s manifest fetch rejects inside asyncLoadProcess (the\neager remote preload) with no catch above it → unhandled rejection → the whole\nNode process exits → Render restarts it → 502 crash loop until the remote wakes.\n\nAdd shell/src/mf-runtime-plugin.ts (wired via module-federation.config.ts\nruntimePlugins):\n- process-level `unhandledRejection` handler so a failed remote never kills the\n  server — routes that don''t touch that remote keep serving\n- `errorLoadRemote` logs which remote failed\n\nFirst load after an idle period still degrades (federated regions error until\nthe remote is warm), but the shell stays up instead of 502-looping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"96a27ffcfb7654c4f169d0cdbfc1cfa054187e42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hakangenc1/MF-Modern.js-v3/git/trees/96a27ffcfb7654c4f169d0cdbfc1cfa054187e42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hakangenc1/MF-Modern.js-v3/git/commits/b37ae74c8f5b70a5968af6b0eb478fed0c22c225","verification":{"payload":null,"