epo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/commits/561972d908bce7132b713cfa0fd111e7a390958a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T17:18:52Z","email":"dylan.storey@gmail.com","name":"Dylan Storey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T18:27:49Z","email":"dylan.storey@gmail.com","name":"Dylan Storey"},"message":"Count a frame against the budget until it has left the page (HLIN-T-0085)\n\nThe page stopped counting a frame the moment it sent `suspend`, so while\nscrolling \"Twenty\" the document held up to eighteen. Now every frame in\nthe document counts, one being suspended included, and room is made\nbefore a frame is mounted: the frame to go is suspended, and the newcomer\nwaits until it has left. Only a frame in view is mounted past twelve, and\nonly when nothing out of view is left to take.\n\nThe SDK answers `suspend` at once with an empty `state` when the module\nregistered no hook or keeps nothing, so a module that keeps nothing costs\nno wait. The twenty measurement now asserts the peak, not the settled\ncount. HLIN-S-0007 *Budget* says both.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y4t8VQeZrx8j1J4qmNuQQT","tree":{"sha":"7d747ade9150ab2dfd339f4c47100bbe837446dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/git/trees/7d747ade9150ab2dfd339f4c47100bbe837446dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/git/commits/561972d908bce7132b713cfa0fd111e7a390958a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6005970?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/u