at was built, found and decided, and the checks\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y4t8VQeZrx8j1J4qmNuQQT","tree":{"sha":"b0413904ba9877b111764adda003fba01a08360a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/git/trees/b0413904ba9877b111764adda003fba01a08360a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/git/commits/cbc3df87e92a55ad577aaa9c6108312733d0d783","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6005970?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dylanbstorey","id":6005970,"login":"dylanbstorey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDU5NzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/colliery-io/hlin/commit/cbc3df87e92a55ad577aaa9c6108312733d0d783","node_id":"C_kwDOUSU9_toAKGNiYzNkZjg3ZTkyYTU1YWQ1NzdhYWE5YzYxMDgzMTI3MzNkMGQ3ODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/colliery-io/hlin/commit/4d3c84e69b0a3fae207a0c546f44d3825e7c5e18","sha":"4d3c84e69b0a3fae207a0c546f44d3825e7c5e18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/commits/4d3c84e69b0a3fae207a0c546f44d3825e7c5e18"}],"sha":"cbc3df87e92a55ad577aaa9c6108312733d0d783","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/commits/cbc3df87e92a55ad577aaa9c6108312733d0d783"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6005970?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dylanbstorey","id":6005970,"login":"dylanbstorey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDU5NzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/commits/4d3c84e69b0a3fae207a0c546f44d3825e7c5e18/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T02:10:05Z","email":"dylan.storey@gmail.com","name":"Dylan Storey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T02:11:28Z","email":"dylan.storey@gmail.com","name":"Dylan Storey"},"message":"Give modules the surface''s context, and keep a surface within its frame budget (HLIN-T-0067)\n\nThe page now tells a mounted module where it is and acts on what it asks:\n\n- `context` whenever the range the shell was asked for or the panel''s own\n  declared parameters move, diffed per frame; `theme` from the chrome''s\n  eleven `--hlin-*` roles as the mounted pack filled them, light or dark as\n  the page''s surface reads.\n- `set-param` (declared parameters only) and `set-range` go through the same\n  handler as the chrome''s controls and a component''s Intent::Select and\n  Intent::Range, so they are stored with the layout and come back as\n  `context`.\n- `navigate` brings a panel on this surface into view; anything else is\n  ignored and logged. `notice` is drawn above the frame as one plain line of\n  at most 140 characters, labelled as the platform''s.\n- `changed` both ways: the page tells its own other modules at once, posts\n  to the shell''s relay, and skips its own echo; a module given up on as\n  unreachable is remounted when its platform reports its panel changed.\n- The budget: at most twelve frames, the least recently seen out of view\n  unmounted first, never one in view, offered `suspend` with its `state`\n  kept in page memory and handed back as `init.restored`.\n\nA panel far down a surface was judged by the ready timeout from when it was\nplaced, not mounted, and would have been given up on before it ever loaded.\nLiveness now starts when the frame does.\n\nThe sample platform (2.3.0) adds `module-context`, the probe on a panel with\na time range and a cluster, and the probe shows everything it is told. Nine\nbrowser tests cover each message, the budget, and a change relayed between\ntwo browser contexts.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y4t8VQeZrx8j1J4qmNuQQT","tree":{"sha":"7a896ef0868f40ad398936265adb6857cad6c306","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/git/trees/7a896ef0868f40ad398936265adb6857cad6c306"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/git/commits/4d3c84e69b0a3fae207a0c546f44d3825e7c5e18","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6005970?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dylanbstorey","id":6005970,"login":"dylanbstorey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDU5NzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/colliery-io/hlin/commit/4d3c84e69b0a3fae207a0c546f44d3825e7c5e18","node_id":"C_kwDOUSU9_toAKDRkM2M4NGU2OWIwYTNmYWUyMDdhMGM1NDZmNDRkMzgyNWU3YzVlMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/colliery-io/hlin/commit/84dcc36c4e0d706f3782c822de229be994e5085d","sha":"84dcc36c4e0d706f3782c822de229be994e5085d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/commits/84dcc36c4e0d706f3782c822de229be994e5085d"}],"sha":"4d3c84e69b0a3fae207a0c546f44d3825e7c5e18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/commits/4d3c84e69b0a3fae207a0c546f44d3825e7c5e18"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6005970?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dylanbstorey","id":6005970,"login":"dylanbstorey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDU5NzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylanbstorey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/commits/84dcc36c4e0d706f3782c822de229be994e5085d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T02:10:00Z","email":"dylan.storey@gmail.com","name":"Dylan Storey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T02:11:28Z","email":"dylan.storey@gmail.com","name":"Dylan Storey"},"message":"Relay what changed to a platform''s modules on every surface (HLIN-T-0067)\n\nA module that writes says `changed`, and the other modules of its platform\nshould refetch, including the ones in other people''s browsers, which the\npage that heard it cannot reach. The page now posts it to\nPOST /api/stream/{surface}/changed, held to the request proxy''s rules for a\nwrite (same-origin, Author, 16 KiB, a layout the caller sees holding a\nmodule of that platform), and the shell puts it on a broadcast beside the\nplatforms'' own event streams.\n\nEvery running surface drains both roads each tick. A module''s change nudges\nthe surface''s shell-drawn instances exactly as a platform event does, and\neither becomes a new `changed` frame on the surface stream where the layout\nshows that platform''s modules. HLIN-S-0003 gains the frame and the endpoint,\nadditively: a browser that does not listen for the event name never sees it.\n\nA surface now follows the events of every platform whose module it shows,\nnot only of pushed panels, since module-only panels are in no aggregator\ninstance, and re-follows when its layout is written.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y4t8VQeZrx8j1J4qmNuQQT","tree":{"sha":"919902caeb9757f7df8bcaff30bd037b86ee6392","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/hlin/git/trees/919902caeb9757f7df8bcaff30bd037b86ee6392"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colliery-io/