url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/c3ba3524eceb003ef46e140df9542e6edd898c79/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T17:06:30Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T17:06:30Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"docs(ios): spec del split en dos targets\n\nDiseña el target `CoreFinancieroKit` (framework estático) que se lleva el\nborde FFI, espejo de `:core-financiero` en Android.\n\nCorrige la premisa con que el PENDING de iOS justificaba esta deuda: el\nsplit NO impone el seam por compilador. El bundle de tests hostea en la\napp, la app enlaza el framework, y los tests de ViewModel tienen que\nimportarlo igual porque `ContractMessages`, `ValidCci` y `DomainError`\nviven ahí. En Android el seam lo cierra el runtime —la JVM no carga la\n`.so`—, no el compilador; iOS no tiene ese mecanismo.\n\nVerificado antes de escribir: xcodeproj 1.27 soporta `objectVersion = 77`\ny los grupos sincronizados, con 12 líneas de diff cosmético en el\nround-trip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7f20d2c5e0648c320dc505b0709e59b4a8a0f745","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/7f20d2c5e0648c320dc505b0709e59b4a8a0f745"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/c3ba3524eceb003ef46e140df9542e6edd898c79","verification":{"payload":"tree 7f20d2c5e0648c320dc505b0709e59b4a8a0f745\nparent 4f3770ba4240991bf1e951920363b0fee8b804ca\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789664790 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789664790 -0500\n\ndocs(ios): spec del split en dos targets\n\nDiseña el target `CoreFinancieroKit` (framework estático) que se lleva el\nborde FFI, espejo de `:core-financiero` en Android.\n\nCorrige la premisa con que el PENDING de iOS justificaba esta deuda: el\nsplit NO impone el seam por compilador. El bundle de tests hostea en la\napp, la app enlaza el framework, y los tests de ViewModel tienen que\nimportarlo igual porque `ContractMessages`, `ValidCci` y `DomainError`\nviven ahí. En Android el seam lo cierra el runtime —la JVM no carga la\n`.so`—, no el compilador; iOS no tiene ese mecanismo.\n\nVerificado antes de escribir: xcodeproj 1.27 soporta `objectVersion = 77`\ny los grupos sincronizados, con 12 líneas de diff cosmético en el\nround-trip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDIU1ECFIO3E7pFyOE8rHBJTFuxUbSjXABXqNvbLVp8+vzlDw3bepzvsz9aIezb/fH\nzrULLVptiNL5htHDDZQAE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T18:14:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohu