hub.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/678762858980b90f2b26e74c2b32524972aba5b4","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKDY3ODc2Mjg1ODk4MGI5MGYyYjI2ZTc0YzJiMzI1MjQ5NzJhYmE1YjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/0e26e330bca057147996a06b6869d0699b4def9c","sha":"0e26e330bca057147996a06b6869d0699b4def9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/0e26e330bca057147996a06b6869d0699b4def9c"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/55ba8b30c39a52db797039d7a7de7fa6c8f1fcc4","sha":"55ba8b30c39a52db797039d7a7de7fa6c8f1fcc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/55ba8b30c39a52db797039d7a7de7fa6c8f1fcc4"}],"sha":"678762858980b90f2b26e74c2b32524972aba5b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/678762858980b90f2b26e74c2b32524972aba5b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/55ba8b30c39a52db797039d7a7de7fa6c8f1fcc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:27:34Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:27:34Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"test(web-angular): cerrar los tres minors del review de las Tareas 10-12\n\n- **`Comisión ITF` y `Total debitado` no tenían `data-testid`**, así que sólo se\n  verificaban mirando el navegador — y son los dos números que la demo compara\n  centavo a centavo entre las cuatro apps. Ahora los tienen y un test los aserta\n  formateados. Va con timers falsos, como su test vecino: la pantalla espera\n  `simulatedLatencyMs` antes de pintar y con `whenStable()` los valores todavía\n  no están en el DOM.\n- **El test de «editar consume el error» cubría sólo `setOrigin`.** Pasa a\n  `it.each` sobre los tres campos: eran idénticos en implementación, y por eso\n  mismo se daban por cubiertos los otros dos.\n- **La llamada re-entrante de `child.value.set(...)`** queda documentada donde\n  ocurre, en `LabeledField.onInput`, con la cadena completa —`onInput` → `model`\n  → handler del padre → `set` del último valor válido— y el argumento de por qué\n  corta en el segundo `set` en vez de ciclar.\n\n**102 tests**, de 99.\n\nY una trampa anotada en el PENDING, que costó una compilación rota: el\n`template` de un componente es un template literal, así que un backtick dentro\nde un comentario HTML lo cierra a la mitad — y el error aparece en `styles:`,\nveinte líneas más abajo, sin ninguna pista de la causa.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6816da833fe971c8d2aa53ef0538d2807d1df4c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/6816da833fe971c8d2aa53ef0538d2807d1df4c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/55ba8b30c39a52db797039d7a7de7fa6c8f1fcc4","verification":{"payload":"tree 6816da833fe971c8d2aa53ef0538d2807d1df4c0\nparent d64577a4276c8e3cd8e69f3f58dbd3cf9cf074a1\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789651654 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789651654 -0500\n\ntest(web-angular): cerrar los tres minors del review de las Tareas 10-12\n\n- **`Comisión ITF` y `Total debitado` no tenían `data-testid`**, así que sólo se\n  verificaban mirando el navegador — y son los dos números que la demo compara\n  centavo a centavo entre las cuatro apps. Ahora los tienen y un test los aserta\n  formateados. Va con timers falsos, como su test vecino: la pantalla espera\n  `simulatedLatencyMs` antes de pintar y con `whenStable()` los valores todavía\n  no están en el DOM.\n- **El test de «editar consume el error» cubría sólo `setOrigin`.** Pasa a\n  `it.each` sobre los tres campos: eran idénticos en implementación, y por eso\n  mismo se daban por cubiertos los otros dos.\n- **La llamada re-entrante de `child.value.set(...)`** queda documentada donde\n  ocurre, en `LabeledField.onInput`, con la cadena completa —`onInput` → `model`\n  → handler del padre → `set` del último valor válido— y el argumento de por qué\n  corta en el segundo `set` en vez de ciclar.\n\n**102 tests**, de 99.\n\nY una trampa anotada en el PENDING, que costó una compilación rota: el\n`template` de un componente es un template literal, así que un backtick dentro\nde un comentario HTML lo cierra a la mitad — y el error aparece en `styles:`,\nveinte líneas más abajo, sin ninguna pista de la causa.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPup8yfMjZP56yOYX0FQQsEvYgpoIemg2hSxFp0G8KFHLbuz01pENr07iDEKVcIjEe\noVhvJhM5uCu9UUOunSygc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/55ba8b30c39a52db797039d7a7de7fa6c8f1fcc4","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKDU1YmE4YjMwYzM5YTUyZGI3OTcwMzlkN2E3ZGU3ZmE2YzhmMWZjYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/d64577a4276c8e3cd8e69f3f58dbd3cf9cf074a1","sha":"d64577a4276c8e3cd8e69f3f58dbd3cf9cf074a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/d64577a4276c8e3cd8e69f3f58dbd3cf9cf074a1"}],"sha":"55ba8b30c39a52db797039d7a7de7fa6c8f1fcc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/55ba8b30c39a52db797039d7a7de7fa6c8f1fcc4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/d64577a4276c8e3cd8e69f3f58dbd3cf9cf074a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:23:31Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:23:31Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"docs(android,ios): poner al día lo que los cambios de la Fase 6 dejaron viejo\n\nLos arreglos de código se commitearon con su prueba, pero la documentación de\nestas dos apps quedó describiendo el estado anterior.\n\n**Android**\n\n- `TESTING.md` listaba **dos** suites y los conteos de antes del módulo\n  `:core-financiero`. Ahora son cuatro, con el reparto real medido: 35 de JVM\n  —31 en `:app` y 4 en `:core-financiero`— y 20 instrumentadas —19 en el módulo,\n  que son las que cargan la librería de verdad, y 1 en `:app`, la rotación—.\n  Cada clase con su número, contado del XML de la corrida.\n- `CONTEXT.md` mostraba el adapter con `runCatching` pelado. Ahora muestra\n  `guarded`, con la nota de por qué existe: `runCatching` atrapa **todo\n  `Throwable`**, así que un fallo de carga de la `.so` vuelve por el mismo camino\n  que un error de negocio, y si no se loguea ahí el diagnóstico se pierde del\n  todo — porque a la pantalla ya no llega.\n\n**iOS**\n\n- `TESTING.md` daba `ContractMessagesTest` en 3 y `BenchmarkViewModelTest` en 6;\n  son 5 y 8. La tabla ahora suma exactamente los 52 de la corrida, verificado.\n- La fila de `Adapter/ContractMessages` del README decía que\n  `localizedDescription` nunca llega a la pantalla; ahora dice también qué pasa\n  con lo que **no** es un `DomainError`, que era el agujero.\n\n**Los diagramas Mermaid de estas dos no cambian, y es a propósito.** Lo que se\nmovió de lugar fue `userMessage` en las apps de TypeScript —de un archivo de cada\napp a `packages/contract`—, y ahí sí se actualizaron los dos diagramas. En\nAndroid e iOS los cambios ocurrieron **dentro** de nodos que ya existen:\n`ContractMessages` ganó una sobrecarga y el adapter un helper. Dibujarlos sería\nruido, no estructura.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0d68b59f99921b294c058c98a041aa118cb8d968","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/0d68b59f99921b294c058c98a041aa118cb8d968"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/d64577a4276c8e3cd8e69f3f58dbd3cf9cf074a1","verification":{"payload":"tree 0d68b59f99921b294c058c98a041aa118cb8d968\nparent 47d850af7ea689639c4abbe8a6a69d70dcdd67c8\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789651411 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789651411 -0500\n\ndocs(android,ios): poner al día lo que los cambios de la Fase 6 dejaron viejo\n\nLos arreglos de código se commitearon con su prueba, pero la documentación de\nestas dos apps quedó describiendo el estado anterior.\n\n**Android**\n\n- `TESTING.md` listaba **dos** suites y los conteos de antes del módulo\n  `:core-financiero`. Ahora son cuatro, con el reparto real medido: 35 de JVM\n  —31 en `:app` y 4 en `:core-financiero`— y 20 instrumentadas —19 en el módulo,\n  que son las que cargan la librería de verdad, y 1 en `:app`, la rotación—.\n  Cada clase con su número, contado del XML de la corrida.\n- `CONTEXT.md` mostraba el adapter con `runCatching` pelado. Ahora muestra\n  `guarded`, con la nota de por qué existe: `runCatching` atrapa **todo\n  `Throwable`**, así que un fallo de carga de la `.so` vuelve por el mismo camino\n  que un error de negocio, y si no se loguea ahí el diagnóstico se pierde del\n  todo — porque a la pantalla ya no llega.\n\n**iOS**\n\n- `TESTING.md` daba `ContractMessagesTest` en 3 y `BenchmarkViewModelTest` en 6;\n  son 5 y 8. La tabla ahora suma exactamente los 52 de la corrida, verificado.\n- La fila de `Adapter/ContractMessages` del README decía que\n  `localizedDescription` nunca llega a la pantalla; ahora dice también qué pasa\n  con lo que **no** es un `DomainError`, que era el agujero.\n\n**Los diagramas Mermaid de estas dos no cambian, y es a propósito.** Lo que se\nmovió de lugar fue `userMessage` en las apps de TypeScript —de un archivo de cada\napp a `packages/contract`—, y ahí sí se actualizaron los dos diagramas. En\nAndroid e iOS los cambios ocurrieron **dentro** de nodos que ya existen:\n`ContractMessages` ganó una sobrecarga y el adapter un helper. Dibujarlos sería\nruido, no estructura.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFzmiWEDtHgoPqD6r3ly6qaM4tMO1C09HhYz4haxH30V3McHGaw8ZK2sUCzBjZnRi+\nX+gGaoy8hvV2XqEbLyfwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/d64577a4276c8e3cd8e69f3f58dbd3cf9cf074a1","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKGQ2NDU3N2E0Mjc2YzhlM2NkOGU2OWYzZjU4ZGJkM2NmOWNmMDc0YTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/47d850af7ea689639c4abbe8a6a69d70dcdd67c8","sha":"47d850af7ea689639c4abbe8a6a69d70dcdd67c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/47d850af7ea689639c4abbe8a6a69d70dcdd67c8"}],"sha":"d64577a4276c8e3cd8e69f3f58dbd3cf9cf074a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/d64577a4276c8e3cd8e69f3f58dbd3cf9cf074a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/47d850af7ea689639c4abbe8a6a69d70dcdd67c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:22:23Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:22:29Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"test(react-native): guardia del @babel/runtime que la pantalla roja encontró\n\nAl cerrar la Fase 5 la app arrancaba en pantalla roja —`Unable to resolve module\n@babel/runtime/helpers/interopRequireDefault from packages/contract/…`— con los\n120 tests en verde. Metro transpila con Babel el TypeScript de los paquetes del\nworkspace consumidos por fuente y resuelve los helpers **relativo al archivo que\ntranspila**, así que bajo el `node_modules` estricto de pnpm el paquete tiene que\ndeclarar `@babel/runtime` él mismo. El arreglo está desde entonces; lo que no\nhabía era nada que lo cazara.\n\nLa guardia deriva de los `package.json` qué paquetes se consumen por fuente —los\nde entrypoint `.ts`— y comprueba que cada uno tenga `node_modules/@babel/runtime`.\n`@banco/core-financiero-wasm` queda fuera solo: su `main` es el bundle de\nesbuild. Y hay un test de que la lista no está vacía, porque una guardia sin\nsujetos es verde y no mira nada.\n\n**Comprueba el filesystem y no el resolver, tras dos intentos fallidos.** Dentro\nde Jest no se puede preguntar si algo resolvería bajo pnpm: Jest parchea\n`Module._resolveFilename` globalmente, así que su `require.resolve` ignora el\n`paths`, y hasta `createRequire` de `node:module` cae en su resolver. Las dos\nvías daban verde para un paquete que NO declara `@babel/runtime`. Se descubrió\nmutando la guardia para incluirlo; con la versión de filesystem esa mutación\nfalla, que es lo único que distingue una guardia de un test decorativo.\n\n**129 tests en verde**, de 127: la guardia suma dos.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c51f0683c8ac8aadb81d0c302d5f3a3387e3751","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/1c51f0683c8ac8aadb81d0c302d5f3a3387e3751"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/47d850af7ea689639c4abbe8a6a69d70dcdd67c8","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c51f0683c8ac8aadb81d0c302d5f3a3387e3751\nparent 2b97bb1a873f69203d37dcb9a59131cfa2b84809\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789651343 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789651349 -0500\n\ntest(react-native): guardia del @babel/runtime que la pantalla roja encontró\n\nAl cerrar la Fase 5 la app arrancaba en pantalla roja —`Unable to resolve module\n@babel/runtime/helpers/interopRequireDefault from packages/contract/…`— con los\n120 tests en verde. Metro transpila con Babel el TypeScript de los paquetes del\nworkspace consumidos por fuente y resuelve los helpers **relativo al archivo que\ntranspila**, así que bajo el `node_modules` estricto de pnpm el paquete tiene que\ndeclarar `@babel/runtime` él mismo. El arreglo está desde entonces; lo que no\nhabía era nada que lo cazara.\n\nLa guardia deriva de los `package.json` qué paquetes se consumen por fuente —los\nde entrypoint `.ts`— y comprueba que cada uno tenga `node_modules/@babel/runtime`.\n`@banco/core-financiero-wasm` queda fuera solo: su `main` es el bundle de\nesbuild. Y hay un test de que la lista no está vacía, porque una guardia sin\nsujetos es verde y no mira nada.\n\n**Comprueba el filesystem y no el resolver, tras dos intentos fallidos.** Dentro\nde Jest no se puede preguntar si algo resolvería bajo pnpm: Jest parchea\n`Module._resolveFilename` globalmente, así que su `require.resolve` ignora el\n`paths`, y hasta `createRequire` de `node:module` cae en su resolver. Las dos\nvías daban verde para un paquete que NO declara `@babel/runtime`. Se descubrió\nmutando la guardia para incluirlo; con la versión de filesystem esa mutación\nfalla, que es lo único que distingue una guardia de un test decorativo.\n\n**129 tests en verde**, de 127: la guardia suma dos.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIHJHnbCEhkVM3lskoVrm3I4pYjGQGMOaQjiuuKdBIIh+mIacPr4UTFtSe93KNskz1\nVMrfkOqcbrYoh/Et2MYwc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/47d850af7ea689639c4abbe8a6a69d70dcdd67c8","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKDQ3ZDg1MGFmN2VhNjg5NjM5YzRhYmJlOGE2YTY5ZDcwZGNkZDY3Yzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/2b97bb1a873f69203d37dcb9a59131cfa2b84809","sha":"2b97bb1a873f69203d37dcb9a59131cfa2b84809","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/2b97bb1a873f69203d37dcb9a59131cfa2b84809"}],"sha":"47d850af7ea689639c4abbe8a6a69d70dcdd67c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/47d850af7ea689639c4abbe8a6a69d70dcdd67c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/2b97bb1a873f69203d37dcb9a59131cfa2b84809/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:17:02Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:17:02Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"refactor(contract): userMessage vive una sola vez, en packages/contract\n\nEstaba escrita **dos veces**, casi idéntica, en\n`apps/react-native/example/src/adapter/ContractMessages.ts` y en\n`apps/web-angular/src/app/core/user-message.ts`, aunque las dos apps ya\ncompartían `packages/contract`. El arreglo del commit anterior —que el texto de\ndiagnóstico dejara de llegar a la pantalla— hubo que aplicarlo en los dos\nlugares, que es exactamente el modo de fallo que una copia duplicada produce.\n\nAhora vive en `packages/contract/src/userMessage.ts`, con `FALLBACK`, y las ocho\nllamadas de producción la importan del barrel. Los dos archivos se borran y los\ndos tests se funden en uno: los objetos de prueba son planos (`tag`/`inner`)\nporque `contractName` discrimina por la presencia de `tag` y no con `instanceOf`\n—Ruling P1 de la Fase 4—, así que el test puede vivir en el paquete, que no\nconoce ningún flavour.\n\nAndroid e iOS mantienen su propia versión porque son otro lenguaje. Lo que\ncomparten las cuatro es el **texto**, normativo en `docs/ui-spec.md`.\n\nReact Native **127** y Angular **99** —bajó de 103 porque sus cuatro specs de\n`userMessage` se mudaron al paquete: la cobertura no se perdió, dejó de estar\nduplicada—. `ng build` verificado: el barrel no arrastra `node:fs` y el bundle\ndel navegador sigue armándose.\n\nDocumentación al día, que es la mitad del entregable:\n\n- **Los dos diagramas Mermaid** —el de React Native y el de Angular— muestran\n  ahora `userMessage` saliendo de `packages/contract` y no de un archivo de la\n  app.\n- Las tablas de piezas de los dos README, el CONTEXT de Angular (su árbol\n  listaba `core/user-message.ts`) y el TESTING de React Native.\n- De paso, el drift de conteos que dejó la v2.4.0 en los ocho documentos de las\n  cuatro apps: los «28 casos» son 31, y los totales por suite son los medidos\n  hoy — Android 31 JVM, iOS 52 en 12 suites, React Native 127 en 16, Angular 99.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"266a7bd48ad7c309601618075c2f299b62c63947","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/266a7bd48ad7c309601618075c2f299b62c63947"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/2b97bb1a873f69203d37dcb9a59131cfa2b84809","verification":{"payload":"tree 266a7bd48ad7c309601618075c2f299b62c63947\nparent f1fb9ecc52dcfa30f54907224240d9f3d43f7599\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789651022 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789651022 -0500\n\nrefactor(contract): userMessage vive una sola vez, en packages/contract\n\nEstaba escrita **dos veces**, casi idéntica, en\n`apps/react-native/example/src/adapter/ContractMessages.ts` y en\n`apps/web-angular/src/app/core/user-message.ts`, aunque las dos apps ya\ncompartían `packages/contract`. El arreglo del commit anterior —que el texto de\ndiagnóstico dejara de llegar a la pantalla— hubo que aplicarlo en los dos\nlugares, que es exactamente el modo de fallo que una copia duplicada produce.\n\nAhora vive en `packages/contract/src/userMessage.ts`, con `FALLBACK`, y las ocho\nllamadas de producción la importan del barrel. Los dos archivos se borran y los\ndos tests se funden en uno: los objetos de prueba son planos (`tag`/`inner`)\nporque `contractName` discrimina por la presencia de `tag` y no con `instanceOf`\n—Ruling P1 de la Fase 4—, así que el test puede vivir en el paquete, que no\nconoce ningún flavour.\n\nAndroid e iOS mantienen su propia versión porque son otro lenguaje. Lo que\ncomparten las cuatro es el **texto**, normativo en `docs/ui-spec.md`.\n\nReact Native **127** y Angular **99** —bajó de 103 porque sus cuatro specs de\n`userMessage` se mudaron al paquete: la cobertura no se perdió, dejó de estar\nduplicada—. `ng build` verificado: el barrel no arrastra `node:fs` y el bundle\ndel navegador sigue armándose.\n\nDocumentación al día, que es la mitad del entregable:\n\n- **Los dos diagramas Mermaid** —el de React Native y el de Angular— muestran\n  ahora `userMessage` saliendo de `packages/contract` y no de un archivo de la\n  app.\n- Las tablas de piezas de los dos README, el CONTEXT de Angular (su árbol\n  listaba `core/user-message.ts`) y el TESTING de React Native.\n- De paso, el drift de conteos que dejó la v2.4.0 en los ocho documentos de las\n  cuatro apps: los «28 casos» son 31, y los totales por suite son los medidos\n  hoy — Android 31 JVM, iOS 52 en 12 suites, React Native 127 en 16, Angular 99.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEuFD4Q/AxCPAuOUJgz2lqtRn/f6DLBerBdXs6EtHUAEqYMTi63+baiSM5ZqF5uicz\n4P7A9fKG72Jn2C2fhAZgk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/2b97bb1a873f69203d37dcb9a59131cfa2b84809","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKDJiOTdiYjFhODczZjY5MjAzZDM3ZGNiOWE1OTEzMWNmYTJiODQ4MDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/f1fb9ecc52dcfa30f54907224240d9f3d43f7599","sha":"f1fb9ecc52dcfa30f54907224240d9f3d43f7599","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/f1fb9ecc52dcfa30f54907224240d9f3d43f7599"}],"sha":"2b97bb1a873f69203d37dcb9a59131cfa2b84809","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/2b97bb1a873f69203d37dcb9a59131cfa2b84809"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/f1fb9ecc52dcfa30f54907224240d9f3d43f7599/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:12:24Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:12:24Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"fix(react-native,web-angular): el diagnóstico deja de llegar a la pantalla\n\nLas dos apps de TypeScript tenían el mismo camino que Android e iOS: el fallback\ndel `catch` devolvía `Ocurrió un error inesperado: ${String(e)}`. El comentario\nde React Native citaba a Android como justificación — y Android lo hacía mal,\ncomo demostró su test rojo.\n\nPasa al texto normativo `No se pudo completar la operación.` y el diagnóstico va\na `console.error`. En Angular eso importa más que en las otras tres: si lo que\nllegó es un trap de WebAssembly, la instancia del módulo queda inutilizable y\ntodas las operaciones siguientes fallan igual hasta recargar la página. Sin la\nconsola, se ve como una app que dejó de responder sin decir por qué.\n\nReact Native **127** y Angular **103**, con las cuatro apps ya alineadas.\n\nQueda anotado en `docs/cross-app-pending.md` lo que este arreglo dejó a la vista:\n`userMessage` está escrita **dos veces**, casi idéntica, en las dos apps de\nTypeScript, aunque ya comparten `packages/contract`. Hubo que corregir las dos,\nque es exactamente el modo de fallo de una copia duplicada.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f1affcdda70398fa063c840726b231dd6a8e01d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/f1affcdda70398fa063c840726b231dd6a8e01d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/f1fb9ecc52dcfa30f54907224240d9f3d43f7599","verification":{"payload":"tree f1affcdda70398fa063c840726b231dd6a8e01d3\nparent df9ef74deb70f9f063e8ebdc2c0f3e1d385fac9e\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789650744 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789650744 -0500\n\nfix(react-native,web-angular): el diagnóstico deja de llegar a la pantalla\n\nLas dos apps de TypeScript tenían el mismo camino que Android e iOS: el fallback\ndel `catch` devolvía `Ocurrió un error inesperado: ${String(e)}`. El comentario\nde React Native citaba a Android como justificación — y Android lo hacía mal,\ncomo demostró su test rojo.\n\nPasa al texto normativo `No se pudo completar la operación.` y el diagnóstico va\na `console.error`. En Angular eso importa más que en las otras tres: si lo que\nllegó es un trap de WebAssembly, la instancia del módulo queda inutilizable y\ntodas las operaciones siguientes fallan igual hasta recargar la página. Sin la\nconsola, se ve como una app que dejó de responder sin decir por qué.\n\nReact Native **127** y Angular **103**, con las cuatro apps ya alineadas.\n\nQueda anotado en `docs/cross-app-pending.md` lo que este arreglo dejó a la vista:\n`userMessage` está escrita **dos veces**, casi idéntica, en las dos apps de\nTypeScript, aunque ya comparten `packages/contract`. Hubo que corregir las dos,\nque es exactamente el modo de fallo de una copia duplicada.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCxoXGKhy0khnxhR28AMl45Av1QcmFHlEsmIaTQIVeF6WCItTyfJ1NcNhs8CTwY01p\nKq7+PXlf3dGmA6nS6jUQU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/f1fb9ecc52dcfa30f54907224240d9f3d43f7599","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKGYxZmI5ZWNjNTJkY2ZhMzBmNTQ5MDcyMjQyNDBkOWYzZDQzZjc1OTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/df9ef74deb70f9f063e8ebdc2c0f3e1d385fac9e","sha":"df9ef74deb70f9f063e8ebdc2c0f3e1d385fac9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/df9ef74deb70f9f063e8ebdc2c0f3e1d385fac9e"}],"sha":"f1fb9ecc52dcfa30f54907224240d9f3d43f7599","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/f1fb9ecc52dcfa30f54907224240d9f3d43f7599"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/df9ef74deb70f9f063e8ebdc2c0f3e1d385fac9e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:11:28Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:11:28Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"fix(android,ios): un fallo que no es de dominio deja de mostrar su diagnóstico\n\nLos cuatro ViewModels de cada app cerraban su manejo de error con el texto crudo\nde la excepción —`?: e.toString()` en Kotlin, `\"\\(error)\"` en Swift—. El PENDING\nde iOS lo daba por **inalcanzable**, «porque el adapter sólo propaga DomainError\ndesde el core». Es falso, y ahora hay un test que lo prueba: `runCatching` de\nKotlin atrapa **todo `Throwable`**, así que un fallo al cargar\n`libcore_financiero.so` o cualquier excepción de JNA vuelve como\n`Result.failure` por el mismo camino. Antes de este commit, el test rojo mostraba\nliteralmente esto en la pantalla de Aritmética:\n\n    java.lang.UnsatisfiedLinkError: dlopen failed: library not found\n\nEl fallback pasa a ser `No se pudo completar la operación.`, normativo en\n`docs/ui-spec.md` e igual en las cuatro apps. **No dice «vuelve a intentarlo» a\npropósito**: si la librería nativa no cargó, reintentar no arregla nada.\n\nEl diagnóstico no se tira, se loguea — y en cada plataforma donde hay un solo\ndueño para hacerlo. En Android, en `UniffiCoreFinanciero`: `runCatching` es el\núnico punto donde se atrapa, así que un `guarded {}` lo cubre todo y\n`ContractMessages` se queda pura, sin dependencia de Android y sin romper los\ntests de JVM. En iOS no existe ese punto —los métodos del protocolo son `throws`\ny cada ViewModel tiene su `catch`—, así que va en la sobrecarga de\n`ContractMessages`. Un error de dominio no se loguea: es el camino normal.\n\nAndroid **31** tests de JVM e iOS **52** en el simulador. Los dos caminos\ncubiertos: el genérico no filtra diagnóstico, y el de dominio sigue dando su\nmensaje —que además es lo que descarta una recursión entre sobrecargas—.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3ec1b0ecd242ccbf1cb9dd17ee5ba2cfe81397cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/3ec1b0ecd242ccbf1cb9dd17ee5ba2cfe81397cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/df9ef74deb70f9f063e8ebdc2c0f3e1d385fac9e","verification":{"payload":"tree 3ec1b0ecd242ccbf1cb9dd17ee5ba2cfe81397cf\nparent c0f8c34dd665eea8b56bfcce46bab724525095d6\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789650688 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789650688 -0500\n\nfix(android,ios): un fallo que no es de dominio deja de mostrar su diagnóstico\n\nLos cuatro ViewModels de cada app cerraban su manejo de error con el texto crudo\nde la excepción —`?: e.toString()` en Kotlin, `\"\\(error)\"` en Swift—. El PENDING\nde iOS lo daba por **inalcanzable**, «porque el adapter sólo propaga DomainError\ndesde el core». Es falso, y ahora hay un test que lo prueba: `runCatching` de\nKotlin atrapa **todo `Throwable`**, así que un fallo al cargar\n`libcore_financiero.so` o cualquier excepción de JNA vuelve como\n`Result.failure` por el mismo camino. Antes de este commit, el test rojo mostraba\nliteralmente esto en la pantalla de Aritmética:\n\n    java.lang.UnsatisfiedLinkError: dlopen failed: library not found\n\nEl fallback pasa a ser `No se pudo completar la operación.`, normativo en\n`docs/ui-spec.md` e igual en las cuatro apps. **No dice «vuelve a intentarlo» a\npropósito**: si la librería nativa no cargó, reintentar no arregla nada.\n\nEl diagnóstico no se tira, se loguea — y en cada plataforma donde hay un solo\ndueño para hacerlo. En Android, en `UniffiCoreFinanciero`: `runCatching` es el\núnico punto donde se atrapa, así que un `guarded {}` lo cubre todo y\n`ContractMessages` se queda pura, sin dependencia de Android y sin romper los\ntests de JVM. En iOS no existe ese punto —los métodos del protocolo son `throws`\ny cada ViewModel tiene su `catch`—, así que va en la sobrecarga de\n`ContractMessages`. Un error de dominio no se loguea: es el camino normal.\n\nAndroid **31** tests de JVM e iOS **52** en el simulador. Los dos caminos\ncubiertos: el genérico no filtra diagnóstico, y el de dominio sigue dando su\nmensaje —que además es lo que descarta una recursión entre sobrecargas—.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNg0SrflFiVZY6+bmgAPaWcUWTQTBTbAsktRqJtXgszwmI6hJk3Wjx1pynh6PO+cO5\nqcjqbx6wT91DVcD0JfFQ0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/df9ef74deb70f9f063e8ebdc2c0f3e1d385fac9e","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKGRmOWVmNzRkZWI3MGY5ZjA2M2U4ZWJkYzJjMGYzZTFkMzg1ZmFjOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/c0f8c34dd665eea8b56bfcce46bab724525095d6","sha":"c0f8c34dd665eea8b56bfcce46bab724525095d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/c0f8c34dd665eea8b56bfcce46bab724525095d6"}],"sha":"df9ef74deb70f9f063e8ebdc2c0f3e1d385fac9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/df9ef74deb70f9f063e8ebdc2c0f3e1d385fac9e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/c0f8c34dd665eea8b56bfcce46bab724525095d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:07:47Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:07:47Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"fix(ios): cerrar las dos divergencias de paridad que quedaban en iOS\n\nLas dos las identificó el bloque 1 de la Fase 6 desde Android, y son de iOS:\n\n- **Con cero iteraciones, iOS era la única de las cuatro que volvía muda.** El\n  `guard … else { return }` evitaba el crash pero el botón no hacía nada y la\n  pantalla parecía rota. Ahora `BenchmarkUiState.error` lleva el texto que\n  `docs/ui-spec.md` volvió normativo —el mismo que ya mostraban Android, React\n  Native y Angular— y una corrida válida lo limpia.\n- **El subtítulo del bloque de pegado se autolistaba**: decía «el hex que\n  produjo la app de iOS, React Native o Angular» estando en iOS. El texto\n  normativo dejó de enumerar plataformas.\n\nY una guardia que **no** es una corrección: los tiempos del benchmark usan punto\ndecimal, y este test existe para que siga siendo así. `String(format:)` de\nFoundation, sin `locale:`, ya es no-localizado; el mismo código en Kotlin hacía\nlo contrario y ésa fue la divergencia que la Fase 6 corrigió en Android. Si\nalguien acá le agrega un `locale:` «para hacerlo bien», reintroduce la\ndivergencia y el test lo caza.\n\n**50 tests en verde** en el simulador iPhone 17, de 48 que eran.\n\nDe paso, una imprecisión propia corregida en `docs/cross-app-pending.md`: decía\nque las otras tres apps tienen que portar la guardia de mutación de `Record`. En\nSwift son `public struct` con campos `var` —tipos de **valor**—, así que mutar\nproduce una copia y la asignación sí se observa: el riesgo no es el mismo y la\nguardia no hace falta ahí.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e6f9d74999e44cb820c88a11c79a79252d090d55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/e6f9d74999e44cb820c88a11c79a79252d090d55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/c0f8c34dd665eea8b56bfcce46bab724525095d6","verification":{"payload":"tree e6f9d74999e44cb820c88a11c79a79252d090d55\nparent eb6818e9037808a52edce945054942a4203c0424\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789650467 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789650467 -0500\n\nfix(ios): cerrar las dos divergencias de paridad que quedaban en iOS\n\nLas dos las identificó el bloque 1 de la Fase 6 desde Android, y son de iOS:\n\n- **Con cero iteraciones, iOS era la única de las cuatro que volvía muda.** El\n  `guard … else { return }` evitaba el crash pero el botón no hacía nada y la\n  pantalla parecía rota. Ahora `BenchmarkUiState.error` lleva el texto que\n  `docs/ui-spec.md` volvió normativo —el mismo que ya mostraban Android, React\n  Native y Angular— y una corrida válida lo limpia.\n- **El subtítulo del bloque de pegado se autolistaba**: decía «el hex que\n  produjo la app de iOS, React Native o Angular» estando en iOS. El texto\n  normativo dejó de enumerar plataformas.\n\nY una guardia que **no** es una corrección: los tiempos del benchmark usan punto\ndecimal, y este test existe para que siga siendo así. `String(format:)` de\nFoundation, sin `locale:`, ya es no-localizado; el mismo código en Kotlin hacía\nlo contrario y ésa fue la divergencia que la Fase 6 corrigió en Android. Si\nalguien acá le agrega un `locale:` «para hacerlo bien», reintroduce la\ndivergencia y el test lo caza.\n\n**50 tests en verde** en el simulador iPhone 17, de 48 que eran.\n\nDe paso, una imprecisión propia corregida en `docs/cross-app-pending.md`: decía\nque las otras tres apps tienen que portar la guardia de mutación de `Record`. En\nSwift son `public struct` con campos `var` —tipos de **valor**—, así que mutar\nproduce una copia y la asignación sí se observa: el riesgo no es el mismo y la\nguardia no hace falta ahí.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQI/0x5u7DieRq9ZkjCe52XEt3IuFAF95fJWLddkpd/nEXRlnsS+Zt7lPnQewZNOks7\nykaoFcF8SroJDhdpnM8gI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/c0f8c34dd665eea8b56bfcce46bab724525095d6","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKGMwZjhjMzRkZDY2NWVlYThiNTZiZmNjZTQ2YmFiNzI0NTI1MDk1ZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/eb6818e9037808a52edce945054942a4203c0424","sha":"eb6818e9037808a52edce945054942a4203c0424","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/eb6818e9037808a52edce945054942a4203c0424"}],"sha":"c0f8c34dd665eea8b56bfcce46bab724525095d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/c0f8c34dd665eea8b56bfcce46bab724525095d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/eb6818e9037808a52edce945054942a4203c0424/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:54:44Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:54:44Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"docs(android): cerrar el bloque 1 — README, CONTEXT, PENDING y lo transversal\n\nLa mitad del entregable, según la regla del repo: una fase no termina con la UI\nandando.\n\n- **`docs/cross-app-pending.md`**, nuevo y dueño único de lo que no es de\n  ninguna app: el benchmark que falta en aparato físico, la ausencia de CI en\n  las cinco bases, el `catch` genérico que muestra diagnóstico como mensaje de\n  usuario, las divergencias de paridad abiertas y la regla de que un `Record` de\n  uniffi se reemplaza y no se muta. Los cuatro `PENDING.md` dejan de repetirlo y\n  apuntan ahí: un tema, un dueño.\n- **El diagrama del README** muestra ahora el camino completo —`rust-core` →\n  generados → `:core-financiero` → `:app` → pantalla— con las cuatro suites\n  colgando de dónde corren, y los comandos llevan los totales que dieron de\n  verdad: 30 y 1 en `:app`, 4 y 19 en `:core-financiero`.\n- **La estructura de `CONTEXT.md`** describía el árbol de un solo módulo con los\n  bindings en `app/src/main/java/uniffi/`.\n- **`docs/ui-spec.md`**: el subtítulo del bloque de pegado deja de listar\n  plataformas —se autolistaba en iOS—, y pasan a ser normativos el mensaje de\n  cero iteraciones y el separador decimal punto de los tiempos del benchmark.\n  Corregir una divergencia en el código y no en la spec la deja volver.\n\nDos mentiras corregidas: el PENDING de Android decía que `ndk.abiFilters` no\nestaba aplicado y lo está hace tiempo; el de React Native declaraba abierta la\nreverificación de Android e iOS, cerrada en la Fase 5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d5a59d490847144acdc0554e36fec3735d112691","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/d5a59d490847144acdc0554e36fec3735d112691"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/eb6818e9037808a52edce945054942a4203c0424","verification":{"payload":"tree d5a59d490847144acdc0554e36fec3735d112691\nparent ecb8fc1e7e2002f2e6b53c89bafbae817f789ff0\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649684 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649684 -0500\n\ndocs(android): cerrar el bloque 1 — README, CONTEXT, PENDING y lo transversal\n\nLa mitad del entregable, según la regla del repo: una fase no termina con la UI\nandando.\n\n- **`docs/cross-app-pending.md`**, nuevo y dueño único de lo que no es de\n  ninguna app: el benchmark que falta en aparato físico, la ausencia de CI en\n  las cinco bases, el `catch` genérico que muestra diagnóstico como mensaje de\n  usuario, las divergencias de paridad abiertas y la regla de que un `Record` de\n  uniffi se reemplaza y no se muta. Los cuatro `PENDING.md` dejan de repetirlo y\n  apuntan ahí: un tema, un dueño.\n- **El diagrama del README** muestra ahora el camino completo —`rust-core` →\n  generados → `:core-financiero` → `:app` → pantalla— con las cuatro suites\n  colgando de dónde corren, y los comandos llevan los totales que dieron de\n  verdad: 30 y 1 en `:app`, 4 y 19 en `:core-financiero`.\n- **La estructura de `CONTEXT.md`** describía el árbol de un solo módulo con los\n  bindings en `app/src/main/java/uniffi/`.\n- **`docs/ui-spec.md`**: el subtítulo del bloque de pegado deja de listar\n  plataformas —se autolistaba en iOS—, y pasan a ser normativos el mensaje de\n  cero iteraciones y el separador decimal punto de los tiempos del benchmark.\n  Corregir una divergencia en el código y no en la spec la deja volver.\n\nDos mentiras corregidas: el PENDING de Android decía que `ndk.abiFilters` no\nestaba aplicado y lo está hace tiempo; el de React Native declaraba abierta la\nreverificación de Android e iOS, cerrada en la Fase 5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAuYnxaeeYyVJW3arNPaVIaKn6xWG4A9XBUI6efWNWfUJMAlYe4o3CgN8o9aqje32s\nmEX67G66mqcpDwiI+OAgw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/eb6818e9037808a52edce945054942a4203c0424","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKGViNjgxOGU5MDM3ODA4YTUyZWRjZTk0NTA1NDk0MmE0MjAzYzA0MjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/ecb8fc1e7e2002f2e6b53c89bafbae817f789ff0","sha":"ecb8fc1e7e2002f2e6b53c89bafbae817f789ff0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/ecb8fc1e7e2002f2e6b53c89bafbae817f789ff0"}],"sha":"eb6818e9037808a52edce945054942a4203c0424","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/eb6818e9037808a52edce945054942a4203c0424"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/ecb8fc1e7e2002f2e6b53c89bafbae817f789ff0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:51:50Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:51:50Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"docs(android): medir el APK de release, que era lo único sin medir del benchmark\n\nLa Fase 2 midió con el APK de debug y anotó que faltaba confirmar si el de\nrelease cambia algo. Se construyeron los dos y se pesaron: 31,2 MiB debug contra\n24,4 MiB release, con el desglose de dónde sale el peso —22,9 MB son los dos\n`classes.dex`; todo lo nativo junto, 1,9 MB, de los cuales 1,4 son los tres\nslices de `libcore_financiero.so`—.\n\nCon una salvedad que hace falta decir: **el release no está minificado**. El\n`buildTypes.release` lleva `optimization { enable = false }`, o sea que R8 no\ncorre, y por eso la diferencia es sólo del 22 %. Citar ese tamaño como «lo que\npesa la app» se equivoca por un factor grande.\n\nLos percentiles en release siguen **sin medir**, y se dice por qué en vez de\ninventar un número: AGP emite el release sin firmar, y el único aparato\ndisponible era un emulador — compararlo contra los 444 µs, que salieron de un\nPixel 6 físico, daría una comparación falsa.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c2589e229e381295ac5203ae8456936bad463802","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/c2589e229e381295ac5203ae8456936bad463802"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/ecb8fc1e7e2002f2e6b53c89bafbae817f789ff0","verification":{"payload":"tree c2589e229e381295ac5203ae8456936bad463802\nparent 38cf770847409122de1d18211a8e6df96c7b626d\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649510 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649510 -0500\n\ndocs(android): medir el APK de release, que era lo único sin medir del benchmark\n\nLa Fase 2 midió con el APK de debug y anotó que faltaba confirmar si el de\nrelease cambia algo. Se construyeron los dos y se pesaron: 31,2 MiB debug contra\n24,4 MiB release, con el desglose de dónde sale el peso —22,9 MB son los dos\n`classes.dex`; todo lo nativo junto, 1,9 MB, de los cuales 1,4 son los tres\nslices de `libcore_financiero.so`—.\n\nCon una salvedad que hace falta decir: **el release no está minificado**. El\n`buildTypes.release` lleva `optimization { enable = false }`, o sea que R8 no\ncorre, y por eso la diferencia es sólo del 22 %. Citar ese tamaño como «lo que\npesa la app» se equivoca por un factor grande.\n\nLos percentiles en release siguen **sin medir**, y se dice por qué en vez de\ninventar un número: AGP emite el release sin firmar, y el único aparato\ndisponible era un emulador — compararlo contra los 444 µs, que salieron de un\nPixel 6 físico, daría una comparación falsa.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQANz5J5L/r6Jit95qH4fuzopWD3d9VsQyq7dgo2n/H12n9BgkN5kGF/beL2As8X95Q\nWUhBxOlutqeIZnqw4zhQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/ecb8fc1e7e2002f2e6b53c89bafbae817f789ff0","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKGVjYjhmYzFlN2UyMDAyZjJlNmI1M2M4OWJhZmJhZTgxN2Y3ODlmZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/38cf770847409122de1d18211a8e6df96c7b626d","sha":"38cf770847409122de1d18211a8e6df96c7b626d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/38cf770847409122de1d18211a8e6df96c7b626d"}],"sha":"ecb8fc1e7e2002f2e6b53c89bafbae817f789ff0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/ecb8fc1e7e2002f2e6b53c89bafbae817f789ff0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/38cf770847409122de1d18211a8e6df96c7b626d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:50:53Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:50:53Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"test(android): el fake usa el hex completo del contrato y se aserta el segundo saldo\n\n- El default de `nextEncrypt` era un hex de 8 caracteres mientras el comentario\n  de `FakeCoreFinanciero` prometía el del contrato. Pasa al de 64 de `tj-001`.\n- `AssetSourcesTest` asertaba id y titular de la segunda cuenta y dejaba sin\n  comprobar el único campo que es dinero. Se agrega el saldo.\n\nEl valor va tomado de `contracts/cases.json`, **no del plan**, que decía\n`\"3200.50\"` cuando el contrato dice `1200.50`. El propio plan manda verificarlo\ncontra el contrato antes de escribirlo, y por eso se cazó: copiarlo habría\nmetido un valor inventado en un test de contrato.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"61c5f73fab3d6ddd728209fed5d4f786f9fc38a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/61c5f73fab3d6ddd728209fed5d4f786f9fc38a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/38cf770847409122de1d18211a8e6df96c7b626d","verification":{"payload":"tree 61c5f73fab3d6ddd728209fed5d4f786f9fc38a7\nparent 128dffe6f3ca12f11b952e78806fd1065ec7026f\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649453 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649453 -0500\n\ntest(android): el fake usa el hex completo del contrato y se aserta el segundo saldo\n\n- El default de `nextEncrypt` era un hex de 8 caracteres mientras el comentario\n  de `FakeCoreFinanciero` prometía el del contrato. Pasa al de 64 de `tj-001`.\n- `AssetSourcesTest` asertaba id y titular de la segunda cuenta y dejaba sin\n  comprobar el único campo que es dinero. Se agrega el saldo.\n\nEl valor va tomado de `contracts/cases.json`, **no del plan**, que decía\n`\"3200.50\"` cuando el contrato dice `1200.50`. El propio plan manda verificarlo\ncontra el contrato antes de escribirlo, y por eso se cazó: copiarlo habría\nmetido un valor inventado en un test de contrato.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCfhvw9AHTDfto6ljBFin/XAUgPzNN+6N8o5gVZMoJVYrVayPjPSN8m4l2ay/LbUAj\nYV7ZE+DfYH7oe2aMEujA8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/38cf770847409122de1d18211a8e6df96c7b626d","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKDM4Y2Y3NzA4NDc0MDkxMjJkZTFkMTgyMTFhOGU2ZGY5NmM3YjYyNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/128dffe6f3ca12f11b952e78806fd1065ec7026f","sha":"128dffe6f3ca12f11b952e78806fd1065ec7026f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/128dffe6f3ca12f11b952e78806fd1065ec7026f"}],"sha":"38cf770847409122de1d18211a8e6df96c7b626d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/38cf770847409122de1d18211a8e6df96c7b626d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/128dffe6f3ca12f11b952e78806fd1065ec7026f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:50:53Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:50:53Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"fix(android): el campo de hex acepta solo [0-9a-f], como manda ui-spec\n\n`docs/ui-spec.md:233` acepta sólo `[0-9a-f]` en `Hex cifrado`, y iOS ya lo\ncumplía con `/^[0-9a-f]*$/`. Android aceptaba `A-F` y las normalizaba con\n`lowercase()`, así que la misma entrada se comportaba distinto en dos apps que\nla demo pone lado a lado. La spec es normativa para las cuatro: cede Android.\n\nSigue siendo un filtro de texto, no una validación — que el hex sea descifrable\nlo decide el core.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a7b03b31331ec79d4d18971acd8563dcea206c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/6a7b03b31331ec79d4d18971acd8563dcea206c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/128dffe6f3ca12f11b952e78806fd1065ec7026f","verification":{"payload":"tree 6a7b03b31331ec79d4d18971acd8563dcea206c2\nparent eaf8097e4966f3cffd159d340d341fbc231e2a3c\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649453 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649453 -0500\n\nfix(android): el campo de hex acepta solo [0-9a-f], como manda ui-spec\n\n`docs/ui-spec.md:233` acepta sólo `[0-9a-f]` en `Hex cifrado`, y iOS ya lo\ncumplía con `/^[0-9a-f]*$/`. Android aceptaba `A-F` y las normalizaba con\n`lowercase()`, así que la misma entrada se comportaba distinto en dos apps que\nla demo pone lado a lado. La spec es normativa para las cuatro: cede Android.\n\nSigue siendo un filtro de texto, no una validación — que el hex sea descifrable\nlo decide el core.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCp53CU7RHgWLtl89e8fGYtXoQh2sle3jD/XWU9M98BlJchDjDTDEZRPPPeaNqSyQB\ntaP1PIN9eErRFceuSW4Ag=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/128dffe6f3ca12f11b952e78806fd1065ec7026f","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKDEyOGRmZmU2ZjNjYTEyZjExYjk1MmU3ODgwNmZkMTA2NWVjNzAyNmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/eaf8097e4966f3cffd159d340d341fbc231e2a3c","sha":"eaf8097e4966f3cffd159d340d341fbc231e2a3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/eaf8097e4966f3cffd159d340d341fbc231e2a3c"}],"sha":"128dffe6f3ca12f11b952e78806fd1065ec7026f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/128dffe6f3ca12f11b952e78806fd1065ec7026f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/eaf8097e4966f3cffd159d340d341fbc231e2a3c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:50:05Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:50:05Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"fix(android): benchmark con locale fijo y mensaje con cero iteraciones\n\nDos divergencias con las otras apps, las dos visibles en la demo:\n\n- **`\"%.2f µs\".format(...)` usa el locale por defecto.** En un aparato es-PE\n  imprime `1,23 µs` mientras React Native, que usa `toFixed(2)`, siempre da\n  `1.23 µs`. Dos pantallas lado a lado con distinto separador decimal rompen la\n  comparación carácter por carácter, que es toda la tesis. Pasa a\n  `String.format(Locale.ROOT, …)`.\n- **Con cero iteraciones Android volvía mudo.** El `?: return` evitaba el\n  spinner colgado pero no decía nada; React Native y Angular ya explicaban.\n  Ahora `BenchmarkUiState.error` lleva el texto —el mismo string exacto que las\n  otras dos— y la pantalla lo pinta con el mismo componente y color que las\n  otras tres.\n\nLos dos tests se escribieron primero y se vieron en rojo.\n\nQueda anotado un hueco de paridad que este bloque no puede cerrar: **iOS es\nahora la única de las cuatro que sigue muda** con cero iteraciones\n(`BenchmarkViewModel.swift:32`, `guard … else { return }`).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1a97895135ebfe10612a751a67d2777714f140e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/1a97895135ebfe10612a751a67d2777714f140e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/eaf8097e4966f3cffd159d340d341fbc231e2a3c","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a97895135ebfe10612a751a67d2777714f140e5\nparent 2fbfc579bf91e78d6f9375ccd4a648e38a2c6cee\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649405 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649405 -0500\n\nfix(android): benchmark con locale fijo y mensaje con cero iteraciones\n\nDos divergencias con las otras apps, las dos visibles en la demo:\n\n- **`\"%.2f µs\".format(...)` usa el locale por defecto.** En un aparato es-PE\n  imprime `1,23 µs` mientras React Native, que usa `toFixed(2)`, siempre da\n  `1.23 µs`. Dos pantallas lado a lado con distinto separador decimal rompen la\n  comparación carácter por carácter, que es toda la tesis. Pasa a\n  `String.format(Locale.ROOT, …)`.\n- **Con cero iteraciones Android volvía mudo.** El `?: return` evitaba el\n  spinner colgado pero no decía nada; React Native y Angular ya explicaban.\n  Ahora `BenchmarkUiState.error` lleva el texto —el mismo string exacto que las\n  otras dos— y la pantalla lo pinta con el mismo componente y color que las\n  otras tres.\n\nLos dos tests se escribieron primero y se vieron en rojo.\n\nQueda anotado un hueco de paridad que este bloque no puede cerrar: **iOS es\nahora la única de las cuatro que sigue muda** con cero iteraciones\n(`BenchmarkViewModel.swift:32`, `guard … else { return }`).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLsw97nHBe5S3P0kuJadw5xm3v4k5At8ovHJqDXEy+lDO+RV1oAl2N/MzmQRDROSll\n/1mJDBHrq5IpiRt1b/lQI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/eaf8097e4966f3cffd159d340d341fbc231e2a3c","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKGVhZjgwOTdlNDk2NmYzY2ZmZDE1OWQzNDBkMzQxZmJjMjMxZTJhM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/2fbfc579bf91e78d6f9375ccd4a648e38a2c6cee","sha":"2fbfc579bf91e78d6f9375ccd4a648e38a2c6cee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/2fbfc579bf91e78d6f9375ccd4a648e38a2c6cee"}],"sha":"eaf8097e4966f3cffd159d340d341fbc231e2a3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/eaf8097e4966f3cffd159d340d341fbc231e2a3c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/2fbfc579bf91e78d6f9375ccd4a648e38a2c6cee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:49:20Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:49:20Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"test(android): guardia contra mutar un Record de uniffi desde la UI\n\nLos cinco `Record` que genera uniffi son `data class` con propiedades `var`, y\nel `@Immutable` de los `UiState` **anula la inferencia** de Compose: si alguien\nescribiera `account.balance = \"0.00\"`, Compose no se enteraría y la pantalla\nseguiría mostrando el saldo viejo. Es corrección, no rendimiento.\n\nLas dos salidas obvias no sirven —los tipos son generados y no se editan, y\nenvolverlos sería duplicar el contrato, que `CONTEXT.md` pone en «Qué NO\nhacer»—, así que la guardia deriva la lista de campos del propio binding y\nregenerar no la pudre.\n\nEl regex va con backticks opcionales, y no es un detalle: uniffi emite\n``var `id`: kotlin.String``, así que el `var\\s+(\\w+)\\s*:` que parecía obvio\ndevuelve un set vacío y la guardia pasa en verde sin mirar un solo campo.\n\n**Vista fallar**, que es lo único que distingue una guardia de un test decorativo:\ncon `account.balance = \"0.00\"` inyectado en `TransferScreen.kt`, falla nombrando\n`TransferScreen.kt:60 → .balance =`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d02c62c7db20600debc8b8e3da0040673de4354b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/d02c62c7db20600debc8b8e3da0040673de4354b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/2fbfc579bf91e78d6f9375ccd4a648e38a2c6cee","verification":{"payload":"tree d02c62c7db20600debc8b8e3da0040673de4354b\nparent c868890506f7fcd2fca197408968042d5dd7b8fd\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649360 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649360 -0500\n\ntest(android): guardia contra mutar un Record de uniffi desde la UI\n\nLos cinco `Record` que genera uniffi son `data class` con propiedades `var`, y\nel `@Immutable` de los `UiState` **anula la inferencia** de Compose: si alguien\nescribiera `account.balance = \"0.00\"`, Compose no se enteraría y la pantalla\nseguiría mostrando el saldo viejo. Es corrección, no rendimiento.\n\nLas dos salidas obvias no sirven —los tipos son generados y no se editan, y\nenvolverlos sería duplicar el contrato, que `CONTEXT.md` pone en «Qué NO\nhacer»—, así que la guardia deriva la lista de campos del propio binding y\nregenerar no la pudre.\n\nEl regex va con backticks opcionales, y no es un detalle: uniffi emite\n``var `id`: kotlin.String``, así que el `var\\s+(\\w+)\\s*:` que parecía obvio\ndevuelve un set vacío y la guardia pasa en verde sin mirar un solo campo.\n\n**Vista fallar**, que es lo único que distingue una guardia de un test decorativo:\ncon `account.balance = \"0.00\"` inyectado en `TransferScreen.kt`, falla nombrando\n`TransferScreen.kt:60 → .balance =`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJu1KNH+LoeVhnu8Diu8wpi1cIEH4qtISrVXx4tksfeaKDkwMuk1S5g+2frnsOrK1a\nOQiDgjeUVTn18kh8cizQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/2fbfc579bf91e78d6f9375ccd4a648e38a2c6cee","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKDJmYmZjNTc5YmY5MWU3OGQ2ZjkzNzVjY2Q0YTY0OGUzOGEyYzZjZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/c868890506f7fcd2fca197408968042d5dd7b8fd","sha":"c868890506f7fcd2fca197408968042d5dd7b8fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/c868890506f7fcd2fca197408968042d5dd7b8fd"}],"sha":"2fbfc579bf91e78d6f9375ccd4a648e38a2c6cee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/2fbfc579bf91e78d6f9375ccd4a648e38a2c6cee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/c868890506f7fcd2fca197408968042d5dd7b8fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:48:38Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:48:38Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"fix(android): la pestaña y el estado sobreviven a la rotación\n\nCon `remember` la rotación se llevaba puesto todo: la app volvía a Aritmética\ncon los campos en blanco. Dos cambios en `BancoApp`:\n\n- La pestaña pasa a `rememberSaveable` sobre el **índice**, no sobre el objeto:\n  `Tab` es un `sealed interface` y guardarlo pediría un `Saver` propio para algo\n  que es un número.\n- Los cuatro ViewModels pasan de `remember` a `viewModel(factory)`, que los ata\n  al `ViewModelStore` de la Activity. Eso exige una factory porque los cuatro\n  tienen dependencias en el constructor: `AppViewModelFactory`, un `when`\n  explícito sin librería de DI, por el mismo motivo que `AppContainer`.\n\nTDD de verdad: `RotationTest` se escribió primero y se verificó **en rojo** —1\ntest, 1 fallo tras `recreate()`— antes de tocar `BancoApp`, y en verde después.\n\nNota de método: el plan manda correr un test instrumentado suelto con\n`--tests ''*RotationTest*''`, y esa opción no existe para `connectedAndroidTest`\n—es de las tareas `Test` de la JVM—. El equivalente real es\n`-Pandroid.testInstrumentationRunnerArguments.class=<FQN>`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aebeb79fa64d11352641ba4b233990baff37a34d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/aebeb79fa64d11352641ba4b233990baff37a34d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/c868890506f7fcd2fca197408968042d5dd7b8fd","verification":{"payload":"tree aebeb79fa64d11352641ba4b233990baff37a34d\nparent f6667af9410b20d8acbbd19d1feda40186c89cc1\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649318 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649318 -0500\n\nfix(android): la pestaña y el estado sobreviven a la rotación\n\nCon `remember` la rotación se llevaba puesto todo: la app volvía a Aritmética\ncon los campos en blanco. Dos cambios en `BancoApp`:\n\n- La pestaña pasa a `rememberSaveable` sobre el **índice**, no sobre el objeto:\n  `Tab` es un `sealed interface` y guardarlo pediría un `Saver` propio para algo\n  que es un número.\n- Los cuatro ViewModels pasan de `remember` a `viewModel(factory)`, que los ata\n  al `ViewModelStore` de la Activity. Eso exige una factory porque los cuatro\n  tienen dependencias en el constructor: `AppViewModelFactory`, un `when`\n  explícito sin librería de DI, por el mismo motivo que `AppContainer`.\n\nTDD de verdad: `RotationTest` se escribió primero y se verificó **en rojo** —1\ntest, 1 fallo tras `recreate()`— antes de tocar `BancoApp`, y en verde después.\n\nNota de método: el plan manda correr un test instrumentado suelto con\n`--tests ''*RotationTest*''`, y esa opción no existe para `connectedAndroidTest`\n—es de las tareas `Test` de la JVM—. El equivalente real es\n`-Pandroid.testInstrumentationRunnerArguments.class=<FQN>`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDjkpeEp5kBjBLvlVpYuYHgNc7S9lNHIgr36tnRTvw1B8PL0KefIAIoJ5yABAc6qYV\n6nWpNX9yhiNDH14ihKaQU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/c868890506f7fcd2fca197408968042d5dd7b8fd","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKGM4Njg4OTA1MDZmN2ZjZDJmY2ExOTc0MDg5NjgwNDJkNWRkN2I4ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/f6667af9410b20d8acbbd19d1feda40186c89cc1","sha":"f6667af9410b20d8acbbd19d1feda40186c89cc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/f6667af9410b20d8acbbd19d1feda40186c89cc1"}],"sha":"c868890506f7fcd2fca197408968042d5dd7b8fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/c868890506f7fcd2fca197408968042d5dd7b8fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/f6667af9410b20d8acbbd19d1feda40186c89cc1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:47:09Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:47:09Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"test(android): el adapter real traduce errores del core a Result.failure\n\nHueco que cierra: `CoreFinancieroAdapterTest` corre en la JVM sobre\n`FakeCoreFinanciero`, y el test de contrato llama a uniffi **directamente**, sin\npasar por el adapter. O sea que ninguna suite comprobaba que el `runCatching` de\n`UniffiCoreFinanciero` convirtiera una excepción del core en `Result.failure`\ncontra la `.so` real; la evidencia era «se forzó un error en el emulador una\nvez».\n\nTres casos, todos instrumentados: la llamada válida vuelve como success; el\nerror del core vuelve como failure y no como throw; y el failure trae un\n`contractName()` con mensaje de usuario no vacío — que es el puente que no cruza\nel FFI, y si se rompe la pantalla de error queda en blanco aunque el core haya\nreportado bien.\n\n`MontoInvalido` no es un valor adivinado: `add` llama a `parse_amount`, que ante\nalgo que no parsea como `Decimal` devuelve `InvalidAmount`, cuyo nombre de\ncontrato es ése.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c9fa7d9635558b35181b9d21232b0274f9c8ad4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/c9fa7d9635558b35181b9d21232b0274f9c8ad4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/f6667af9410b20d8acbbd19d1feda40186c89cc1","verification":{"payload":"tree c9fa7d9635558b35181b9d21232b0274f9c8ad4b\nparent acb4c953e2e41d2e45e1921d84f72c2fbd7dad04\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649229 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649229 -0500\n\ntest(android): el adapter real traduce errores del core a Result.failure\n\nHueco que cierra: `CoreFinancieroAdapterTest` corre en la JVM sobre\n`FakeCoreFinanciero`, y el test de contrato llama a uniffi **directamente**, sin\npasar por el adapter. O sea que ninguna suite comprobaba que el `runCatching` de\n`UniffiCoreFinanciero` convirtiera una excepción del core en `Result.failure`\ncontra la `.so` real; la evidencia era «se forzó un error en el emulador una\nvez».\n\nTres casos, todos instrumentados: la llamada válida vuelve como success; el\nerror del core vuelve como failure y no como throw; y el failure trae un\n`contractName()` con mensaje de usuario no vacío — que es el puente que no cruza\nel FFI, y si se rompe la pantalla de error queda en blanco aunque el core haya\nreportado bien.\n\n`MontoInvalido` no es un valor adivinado: `add` llama a `parse_amount`, que ante\nalgo que no parsea como `Decimal` devuelve `InvalidAmount`, cuyo nombre de\ncontrato es ése.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLi44m6XGAWwtm7Qaxdg+TSegvy3K2ixS512qp6bCqlVleBl5wdgy6iT5+EoIWOvo7\nqJhgUqQ/MkuYaMkHFhKw4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/f6667af9410b20d8acbbd19d1feda40186c89cc1","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKGY2NjY3YWY5NDEwYjIwZDhhY2JiZDE5ZDFmZWRhNDAxODZjODljYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/acb4c953e2e41d2e45e1921d84f72c2fbd7dad04","sha":"acb4c953e2e41d2e45e1921d84f72c2fbd7dad04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/acb4c953e2e41d2e45e1921d84f72c2fbd7dad04"}],"sha":"f6667af9410b20d8acbbd19d1feda40186c89cc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/f6667af9410b20d8acbbd19d1feda40186c89cc1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/acb4c953e2e41d2e45e1921d84f72c2fbd7dad04/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:37:38Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:37:38Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"test(android): repartir las suites entre :app y :core-financiero\n\nEl test de contrato, el smoke del FFI y el de las fuentes de assets se van al\nandroidTest de `:core-financiero`, que es donde el `Copy` de contratos deja los\nJSON desde la tarea anterior; el del mapeo de mensajes, a su suite JVM. En\n`:app` quedan los que prueban presentación: los cuatro de ViewModel con\n`FakeCoreFinanciero`, `MoneyFormatterTest` y `NativeBaselineTest`.\n\n`AssetSourcesTest` pasa de `targetContext` a `context`: el `targetContext` de\nuna librería no es la app, y con él `open(\"cases.json\")` tira\nFileNotFoundException.\n\nNingún test se perdió en la mudanza. JVM: 25 en `:app` + 4 en `:core-financiero`\n= los mismos 29. Instrumentada: los mismos 16, ahora en `:core-financiero`, y\ncierra el rojo que dejó el commit anterior.\n\nQueda una consecuencia para las tareas 5 y 6: el androidTest de `:app` quedó\nvacío, así que `:app:connectedDebugAndroidTest` pasa sin correr un solo test.\nLo cierran la rotación y la guardia del `@Immutable`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"76b9ced0f4c49173acd0ce63bf71aa53864ac0b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/76b9ced0f4c49173acd0ce63bf71aa53864ac0b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/acb4c953e2e41d2e45e1921d84f72c2fbd7dad04","verification":{"payload":"tree 76b9ced0f4c49173acd0ce63bf71aa53864ac0b8\nparent 7c792c4cf33af939a1cd01686e3ca915db957144\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789648658 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789648658 -0500\n\ntest(android): repartir las suites entre :app y :core-financiero\n\nEl test de contrato, el smoke del FFI y el de las fuentes de assets se van al\nandroidTest de `:core-financiero`, que es donde el `Copy` de contratos deja los\nJSON desde la tarea anterior; el del mapeo de mensajes, a su suite JVM. En\n`:app` quedan los que prueban presentación: los cuatro de ViewModel con\n`FakeCoreFinanciero`, `MoneyFormatterTest` y `NativeBaselineTest`.\n\n`AssetSourcesTest` pasa de `targetContext` a `context`: el `targetContext` de\nuna librería no es la app, y con él `open(\"cases.json\")` tira\nFileNotFoundException.\n\nNingún test se perdió en la mudanza. JVM: 25 en `:app` + 4 en `:core-financiero`\n= los mismos 29. Instrumentada: los mismos 16, ahora en `:core-financiero`, y\ncierra el rojo que dejó el commit anterior.\n\nQueda una consecuencia para las tareas 5 y 6: el androidTest de `:app` quedó\nvacío, así que `:app:connectedDebugAndroidTest` pasa sin correr un solo test.\nLo cierran la rotación y la guardia del `@Immutable`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDXQa66Z/jqlDUrVm61oGo5VVXkKROC1/mJ3WYZu3UDSfTE1KcCK/ieRhSUedOKY48\nJMkKUp+h4zRmqCe3JXow0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/acb4c953e2e41d2e45e1921d84f72c2fbd7dad04","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKGFjYjRjOTUzZTJlNDFkMmU0NWUxOTIxZDg0ZjcyYzJmYmQ3ZGFkMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/7c792c4cf33af939a1cd01686e3ca915db957144","sha":"7c792c4cf33af939a1cd01686e3ca915db957144","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/7c792c4cf33af939a1cd01686e3ca915db957144"}],"sha":"acb4c953e2e41d2e45e1921d84f72c2fbd7dad04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/acb4c953e2e41d2e45e1921d84f72c2fbd7dad04"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/7c792c4cf33af939a1cd01686e3ca915db957144/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:36:53Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:36:53Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"refactor(android): el adapter y las fuentes del contrato pasan a :core-financiero\n\n`adapter/` y `contract/` se mudan al módulo con `git mv`, conservando su paquete\n—`dev.tohure.android_rust_test.*`—, así que ningún `import` de `:app` cambió: el\n`namespace` de un módulo Android es para el `R` y el `BuildConfig`, no para los\npaquetes de las fuentes. El bloque `Copy` de `contracts/*.json` se muda con\nellos; los assets de una librería se mergean en el APK de la app, verificado:\n`cases.json` y `messages.es.json` siguen dentro de `app-debug.apk`.\n\nEl Step 4 del plan esperaba cero `import uniffi.*` en `app/src/main` y quedan\ncuatro TIPOS —`Account`, `DomainException`, `TransferRequest`,\n`TransferResult`—. No es deuda: `CoreFinanciero.kt` documenta que el adapter\nreexporta los tipos del core y no los traduce, y `CONTEXT.md:332` lo pone en la\ntabla de «Qué NO hacer». Lo que sí se verificó es que `:app` no llama a una sola\nfunción del core: la única referencia a la implementación es `AppContainer`\nconstruyendo `UniffiCoreFinanciero()`, que es el composition root.\n\n**Este commit deja la suite instrumentada de `:app` en rojo**, 11 de 16, y es\nesperado: el `Copy` de test alimenta ahora el APK de test del módulo, así que el\nde `:app` se quedó sin los JSON. La Task 3 lo cierra moviendo esos tests a donde\nestán los assets. La suite JVM sigue en verde, 29/29.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"89f087ae3531fcc8b6ee2b32ff2ce0121ff62609","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/89f087ae3531fcc8b6ee2b32ff2ce0121ff62609"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/7c792c4cf33af939a1cd01686e3ca915db957144","verification":{"payload":"tree 89f087ae3531fcc8b6ee2b32ff2ce0121ff62609\nparent 4958a4d7eea80acf1f31e546514138cc19974e0c\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789648613 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789648613 -0500\n\nrefactor(android): el adapter y las fuentes del contrato pasan a :core-financiero\n\n`adapter/` y `contract/` se mudan al módulo con `git mv`, conservando su paquete\n—`dev.tohure.android_rust_test.*`—, así que ningún `import` de `:app` cambió: el\n`namespace` de un módulo Android es para el `R` y el `BuildConfig`, no para los\npaquetes de las fuentes. El bloque `Copy` de `contracts/*.json` se muda con\nellos; los assets de una librería se mergean en el APK de la app, verificado:\n`cases.json` y `messages.es.json` siguen dentro de `app-debug.apk`.\n\nEl Step 4 del plan esperaba cero `import uniffi.*` en `app/src/main` y quedan\ncuatro TIPOS —`Account`, `DomainException`, `TransferRequest`,\n`TransferResult`—. No es deuda: `CoreFinanciero.kt` documenta que el adapter\nreexporta los tipos del core y no los traduce, y `CONTEXT.md:332` lo pone en la\ntabla de «Qué NO hacer». Lo que sí se verificó es que `:app` no llama a una sola\nfunción del core: la única referencia a la implementación es `AppContainer`\nconstruyendo `UniffiCoreFinanciero()`, que es el composition root.\n\n**Este commit deja la suite instrumentada de `:app` en rojo**, 11 de 16, y es\nesperado: el `Copy` de test alimenta ahora el APK de test del módulo, así que el\nde `:app` se quedó sin los JSON. La Task 3 lo cierra moviendo esos tests a donde\nestán los assets. La suite JVM sigue en verde, 29/29.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGNHA2De3qt7ONjOTP4F1Hhs3Yljex/Eh4B1hIlJXTZ+8Lvk1hH3yZm3hm/zehct+1\nLvV7ZauW/yrDS/19KUpg0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/7c792c4cf33af939a1cd01686e3ca915db957144","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKDdjNzkyYzRjZjMzYWY5MzlhMWNkMDE2ODZlM2NhOTE1ZGI5NTcxNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/4958a4d7eea80acf1f31e546514138cc19974e0c","sha":"4958a4d7eea80acf1f31e546514138cc19974e0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/4958a4d7eea80acf1f31e546514138cc19974e0c"}],"sha":"7c792c4cf33af939a1cd01686e3ca915db957144","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/7c792c4cf33af939a1cd01686e3ca915db957144"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/4958a4d7eea80acf1f31e546514138cc19974e0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:27:23Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:27:23Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"refactor(android): módulo :core-financiero con los generados en su propio source set\n\nNace `:core-financiero` como Android Library y se lleva JNA, los bindings\ngenerados y las `.so`. `:app` deja de declarar JNA. Las tareas 2 y 3 mudan el\nadapter y reparten las suites.\n\nTres cosas que el plan daba por ciertas y no lo eran:\n\n- **Los generados no están versionados**, están ignorados por `.gitignore`. No\n  hay `git mv` posible, el `.gitattributes` con `linguist-generated` no aplica a\n  archivos no trackeados, y verificar la mudanza con `git diff` no verifica\n  nada. Se movieron con `mv`, se actualizaron las dos rutas del `.gitignore`, y\n  la verificación es el SHA embebido en el `.so`: `1.0.0+959025f` antes y\n  después, así que el pie de `coreVersion()` no se movió.\n- **`java.srcDir` deja los `.kt` fuera del compilador de Kotlin** con el Kotlin\n  integrado de AGP 9. El módulo compilaba «bien», el AAR salía con las `.so`\n  adentro, y el jar traía una sola clase —el `R`—; el fallo aparecía a un módulo\n  de distancia, como `Unresolved reference ''DomainException''` en los\n  ViewModels. Con `kotlin.srcDir`, 98 clases.\n- **`com.android.library` hay que declararlo en el build raíz** con\n  `apply false`, o el alias del módulo no resuelve.\n\nMover los generados cambia la ruta de salida de la regeneración, así que se\ncorrigen los comandos en `rust-core/CONTEXT.md` (la fuente única),\n`rust-core/BUILD.md`, `rust-core/README.md` y los ocho de\n`apps/android/BUILD.md` y `README.md`. Sin eso, el próximo que regenere deja los\nartefactos en la ruta vieja y la app compila en silencio contra lo que quedó.\n\nVerificado: `clean` + `:app:assembleDebug` en verde, el APK con las tres `.so`,\nJVM 29/29 e instrumentada 16/16 —incluida `theLibraryLoadsAndJnaResolvesSymbols`,\nque prueba que el `.so` carga desde el AAR del módulo—.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3a45af17ed7da6c4408b7788370362b1cb7b6c47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/3a45af17ed7da6c4408b7788370362b1cb7b6c47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/4958a4d7eea80acf1f31e546514138cc19974e0c","verification":{"payload":"tree 3a45af17ed7da6c4408b7788370362b1cb7b6c47\nparent 391a1861652d3ad9d8e10a64c6b6235c8ae96d44\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789648043 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789648043 -0500\n\nrefactor(android): módulo :core-financiero con los generados en su propio source set\n\nNace `:core-financiero` como Android Library y se lleva JNA, los bindings\ngenerados y las `.so`. `:app` deja de declarar JNA. Las tareas 2 y 3 mudan el\nadapter y reparten las suites.\n\nTres cosas que el plan daba por ciertas y no lo eran:\n\n- **Los generados no están versionados**, están ignorados por `.gitignore`. No\n  hay `git mv` posible, el `.gitattributes` con `linguist-generated` no aplica a\n  archivos no trackeados, y verificar la mudanza con `git diff` no verifica\n  nada. Se movieron con `mv`, se actualizaron las dos rutas del `.gitignore`, y\n  la verificación es el SHA embebido en el `.so`: `1.0.0+959025f` antes y\n  después, así que el pie de `coreVersion()` no se movió.\n- **`java.srcDir` deja los `.kt` fuera del compilador de Kotlin** con el Kotlin\n  integrado de AGP 9. El módulo compilaba «bien», el AAR salía con las `.so`\n  adentro, y el jar traía una sola clase —el `R`—; el fallo aparecía a un módulo\n  de distancia, como `Unresolved reference ''DomainException''` en los\n  ViewModels. Con `kotlin.srcDir`, 98 clases.\n- **`com.android.library` hay que declararlo en el build raíz** con\n  `apply false`, o el alias del módulo no resuelve.\n\nMover los generados cambia la ruta de salida de la regeneración, así que se\ncorrigen los comandos en `rust-core/CONTEXT.md` (la fuente única),\n`rust-core/BUILD.md`, `rust-core/README.md` y los ocho de\n`apps/android/BUILD.md` y `README.md`. Sin eso, el próximo que regenere deja los\nartefactos en la ruta vieja y la app compila en silencio contra lo que quedó.\n\nVerificado: `clean` + `:app:assembleDebug` en verde, el APK con las tres `.so`,\nJVM 29/29 e instrumentada 16/16 —incluida `theLibraryLoadsAndJnaResolvesSymbols`,\nque prueba que el `.so` carga desde el AAR del módulo—.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPLrDsJFaDv4OgVJqWNaL9S57jqo40MWNXzhRynMvmldGhkNjcS83zo5wemWgZbBzq\nMse02MuJJV9DCilRDI9wY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/4958a4d7eea80acf1f31e546514138cc19974e0c","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKDQ5NThhNGQ3ZWVhODBhY2YxZjMxZTU0NjUxNDEzOGNjMTk5NzRlMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/391a1861652d3ad9d8e10a64c6b6235c8ae96d44","sha":"391a1861652d3ad9d8e10a64c6b6235c8ae96d44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/391a1861652d3ad9d8e10a64c6b6235c8ae96d44"}],"sha":"4958a4d7eea80acf1f31e546514138cc19974e0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/4958a4d7eea80acf1f31e546514138cc19974e0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/391a1861652d3ad9d8e10a64c6b6235c8ae96d44/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:23:21Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:23:21Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"docs: el pie va pelado, y leer los cuatro sin mirarlos a ojo\n\nDos correcciones que salieron de verificar el pie de las cuatro apps en la\nFase 6, y que existen para que la confusión de esa corrida no se repita.\n\n**ui-spec.md** dibujaba el pie como `core 1.0.0 · a0a40a5`: con prefijo y con\n`·`. Ninguna de las cuatro apps renderiza eso, y contradecía a su propia regla\nnormativa de la sección 5 («sin reformatear»). No era cosmético — iOS llegó a\nanteponer `\"core \"` siguiendo este dibujo, y con builds idénticos los dos pies\nno eran el mismo string, que es lo único que este pie existe para probar.\n\n**demo-runbook.md** pedía «abrir cada app y mirar el pie». Comparar cuatro\nstrings de trece caracteres a ojo es justo lo que el ojo hace mal, y en la\nFase 6 dio una falsa alarma. Se agregan los comandos que leen el TEXTO\nRENDERIZADO de cada app —`uiautomator dump` para Android y React Native,\n`simctl io screenshot` para iOS, Chrome headless con `--dump-dom` para\nAngular—, los cuatro ejecutados tal como están escritos.\n\nY las tres trampas que produjeron esa falsa alarma, las tres verificadas:\n`connectedAndroidTest` desinstala las dos APK al terminar; el snapshot del\nemulador restaura apps de sesiones viejas y hay dos paquetes con nombre\nparecido (la Android nativa y la de React Native); y el simulador de iOS se\nqueda con el último build, no con el último artefacto.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"22d6ee15c18eabfc22ddc866b2fe4e35aabfa8e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/22d6ee15c18eabfc22ddc866b2fe4e35aabfa8e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/391a1861652d3ad9d8e10a64c6b6235c8ae96d44","verification":{"payload":"tree 22d6ee15c18eabfc22ddc866b2fe4e35aabfa8e2\nparent 1c3a687100f669cf9dc796823a61dcc8b37fc41a\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789647801 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789647801 -0500\n\ndocs: el pie va pelado, y leer los cuatro sin mirarlos a ojo\n\nDos correcciones que salieron de verificar el pie de las cuatro apps en la\nFase 6, y que existen para que la confusión de esa corrida no se repita.\n\n**ui-spec.md** dibujaba el pie como `core 1.0.0 · a0a40a5`: con prefijo y con\n`·`. Ninguna de las cuatro apps renderiza eso, y contradecía a su propia regla\nnormativa de la sección 5 («sin reformatear»). No era cosmético — iOS llegó a\nanteponer `\"core \"` siguiendo este dibujo, y con builds idénticos los dos pies\nno eran el mismo string, que es lo único que este pie existe para probar.\n\n**demo-runbook.md** pedía «abrir cada app y mirar el pie». Comparar cuatro\nstrings de trece caracteres a ojo es justo lo que el ojo hace mal, y en la\nFase 6 dio una falsa alarma. Se agregan los comandos que leen el TEXTO\nRENDERIZADO de cada app —`uiautomator dump` para Android y React Native,\n`simctl io screenshot` para iOS, Chrome headless con `--dump-dom` para\nAngular—, los cuatro ejecutados tal como están escritos.\n\nY las tres trampas que produjeron esa falsa alarma, las tres verificadas:\n`connectedAndroidTest` desinstala las dos APK al terminar; el snapshot del\nemulador restaura apps de sesiones viejas y hay dos paquetes con nombre\nparecido (la Android nativa y la de React Native); y el simulador de iOS se\nqueda con el último build, no con el último artefacto.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGgsMef+RK9Pf/IT5YX9RZNE8R0V4cMgYCgtr4oE4CzBZVsWGUwlCPXKRxmkc1xncI\nXhhVVaqlxZEj6YGjHo0Q0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","f