URE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/959025fccb29e50b8f96bffa64074a412d8e2921","node_id":"C_kwDOUS7obdoAKDk1OTAyNWZjY2IyOWU1MGI4Zjk2YmZmYTY0MDc0YTQxMmQ4ZTI5MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commit/21ee36fa68d40615bf0bfb7d00581fdf1d539750","sha":"21ee36fa68d40615bf0bfb7d00581fdf1d539750","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/21ee36fa68d40615bf0bfb7d00581fdf1d539750"}],"sha":"959025fccb29e50b8f96bffa64074a412d8e2921","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/959025fccb29e50b8f96bffa64074a412d8e2921"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tohure","id":11746842,"login":"tohure","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzQ2ODQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tohure","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/commits/21ee36fa68d40615bf0bfb7d00581fdf1d539750/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:04:36Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:04:36Z","email":"11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Carlo Huamán"},"message":"docs(rust-core): comprobar los seis artefactos de una vez, y el regex que miente\n\nEl README explicaba que hay que regenerar los cuatro artefactos desde el mismo\nHEAD, pero sólo daba el comando para el `.dylib` del host: la comprobación que\nde verdad importa antes de la demo —que los cuatro coincidan entre sí— había que\narmarla a mano.\n\nSe agrega el bucle sobre los seis binarios (Android, los dos slices de iOS, el\nturbo module, el N-API y el WASM) con su salida real, y la trampa que apareció\nal correrlo en la Fase 6: **el patrón va anclado al SHA de HEAD, nunca abierto\ncomo `[0-9a-f]{7,}`**. Rust empaqueta los literales de string contiguos y sin\nterminador, así que `strings` los devuelve pegados y un patrón abierto se come\nlos caracteres hex del literal siguiente — `1.0.0+56acc05ca` en un binario y\n`1.0.0+56acc05` en otro, siendo los dos del mismo commit. El `ca` era el\nprincipio de \"called `Result::unwrap()`\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8066411d2ad6a11e798c1a359ab0d2612feefe6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/trees/8066411d2ad6a11e798c1a359ab0d2612feefe6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tohure/rust-core-cross-app/git/commits/21ee36fa68d40615bf0bfb7d00581fdf1d539750","verification":{"payload":"tree 8066411d2ad6a11e798c1a359ab0d2612feefe6a\nparent 56acc05a924a020ba99735a37d6d19755529ca29\nauthor Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789646676 -0500\ncommitter Carlo Huamán <11746842+tohure@users.noreply.github.com> 1789646676 -0500\n\ndocs(rust-core): comprobar los seis artefactos de una vez, y el regex que miente\n\nEl README explicaba que hay que regenerar los cuatro artefactos desde el mismo\nHEAD, pero sólo daba el comando para el `.dylib` del host: la comprobación que\nde verdad importa antes de la demo —que los cuatro coincidan entre sí— había que\narmarla a mano.\n\nSe agrega el bucle sobre los seis binarios (Android, los dos slices de iOS, el\nturbo module, el N-API y el WASM) con su salida real, y la trampa que apareció\nal correrlo en la Fase 6: **el patrón va anclado al SHA de HEAD, nunca abierto\ncomo `[0-9a-f]{7,}`**. Rust empaqueta los literales de string contiguos y sin\nterminador, así que `strings` los devuelve pegados y un patrón abierto se come\nlos caracteres hex del literal siguiente — `1.0.0+56acc05ca` en un binario y\n`1.0.0+56acc05` en otro, siendo los dos del mismo commit. El `ca` era el\nprincipio de \"called `Result::unwrap()`\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYwo/ItiWFOwhIDQ4kB3xMHezGh\nT5/ikeR/s+7VPfnxwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKvUZW8K8PvAII+wBYX3oxmH3odPFiCtovLEC9YlMsGdpuowiU+Dpjke3emtp+a4xG\nH7LjZVLZrzQr7tddHu1ws=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T15:57:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11746842?v=4","events_url":